- Audio quality
- Effective use of visual material', 'deliverable', 'recommended', 'ms1', 'MS1-6', true, '[{"op": "max", "value": 25.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 25.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 15.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 15.0, "unit": "points"}]'::jsonb),
  ('F.8.3.4', 'F.8.3.4', 'F', 8, 'Ms1 6Th Milestone, Pitch Presentation', 'Evaluation and scoring', 'DOCS', 'These values represent the approximate weight of each dimension but do not imply that the milestone will be evaluated strictly by sections.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-6', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.8.3.5', 'F.8.3.5', 'F', 8, 'Ms1 6Th Milestone, Pitch Presentation', 'Evaluation and scoring', 'DOCS', 'The jury will assign a global score based on the overall quality, clarity and impact of the pitch presentation.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-6', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.1.1', 'F.9.1.1', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Milestone preamble', 'DOCS', 'This milestone consists of a formal presentation delivered during the Final Event in front of an international jury composed of professionals from the motorsport, mobility and engineering industries.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.1.2', 'F.9.1.2', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Milestone preamble', 'DOCS', 'The Final Presentation represents the closing moment of the MS1 phase and provides the team with the opportunity to present the overall development of the project and the final prototype built for the competition.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.1.3', 'F.9.1.3', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Milestone preamble', 'DOCS', 'The objective of this milestone is to allow the jury to understand the engineering process followed by the team, the main technical decisions taken during the project and the results achieved.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.1.4', 'F.9.1.4', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Milestone preamble', 'DOCS', 'Special attention should be given to the evolution of the project, including the differences between the initially proposed concept and the final prototype presented at the event. Teams are encouraged to explain the reasons behind any relevant design, manufacturing or economic deviations.', 'process', 'recommended', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.1.5', 'F.9.1.5', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Milestone preamble', 'DOCS', 'This presentation should demonstrate the team’s capacity to clearly communicate complex engineering work to a professional audience.', 'process', 'recommended', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.1.6', 'F.9.1.6', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Milestone preamble', 'DOCS', 'The Final Presentation may also serve as an opportunity for teams to interact with industry professionals and potential future employers present at the event.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.2.1', 'F.9.2.1', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Presentation format', 'DOCS', 'The presentation will take place during the Final Event according to the schedule defined by the Organization.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.2.2', 'F.9.2.2', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Presentation format', 'DOCS', 'The maximum duration of the presentation will be 30 minutes.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.2.3', 'F.9.2.3', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Presentation format', 'DOCS', 'The jury may ask questions during the presentation. After the presentation, the jury may continue the discussion with the team in the team’s box in the presence of the prototype.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.2.4', 'F.9.2.4', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Presentation format', 'DOCS', 'A maximum of three students may deliver the presentation. Other team members, the Team Leader and the Team Tutors may attend the presentation but may not intervene during the exposition.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.2.5', 'F.9.2.5', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Presentation format', 'DOCS', 'A digital screen with HDMI connection will be provided by the Organization. Presenting students must bring their own laptop and the required adapters or chargers. Internet connection will not be guaranteed during the Final Event. Teams are responsible for ensuring that their presentation materials can run offline.', 'process', 'required', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.3.1', 'F.9.3.1', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Section1: Product definition and project evolution', 'DOCS', 'The objective of this section is to explain the definition of the prototype and the development process followed by the team during the competition.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.3.2', 'F.9.3.2', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Section1: Product definition and project evolution', 'DOCS', 'The presentation should highlight the main engineering decisions taken during the design and manufacturing of the prototype. Teams should explain how the initial concept evolved during the project and describe any relevant deviations from the original design presented in the MS1 milestones. These deviations may include design modifications, manufacturing challenges, changes in materials or adjustments required to achieve a functional prototype.', 'process', 'recommended', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.3.3', 'F.9.3.3', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Section1: Product definition and project evolution', 'DOCS', 'The objective of this section is not only to present the final prototype but also to demonstrate the engineering reasoning and problem-solving capabilities of the team.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.4.1', 'F.9.4.1', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Section 2: Innovation project', 'DOCS', 'The objective of this section is to present the innovation project developed by the team during the competition.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.4.2', 'F.9.4.2', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Section 2: Innovation project', 'DOCS', 'Teams must explain the motivation behind the selected innovation and how it contributes to improving the prototype. The presentation should describe the development process of the innovation, the decisions taken during the project and the validation methods used. If the innovation has been integrated into the final prototype, the team should clearly demonstrate how it operates and what impact it has on the vehicle performance or project objectives.', 'process', 'required', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.4.3', 'F.9.4.3', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Section 2: Innovation project', 'DOCS', 'The jury may ask additional questions regarding the technical feasibility, development process and potential impact of the innovation.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.5.1', 'F.9.5.1', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Evaluation and scoring', 'DOCS', 'The maximum score for this milestone is 60 points.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.5.2', 'F.9.5.2', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Evaluation and scoring', 'DOCS', 'The milestone will be evaluated as a whole, considering the clarity of the presentation, the engineering reasoning shown by the team and the ability to communicate the project to a professional audience. Although teams are free to structure their presentation as they consider appropriate, the evaluation will consider several key dimensions of the project.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.5.3', 'F.9.5.3', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Evaluation and scoring', 'DOCS', 'The maximum weight of each dimension and the aspects that may be considered by the jury include:
1) Product definition and project evolution (maximum 25 points)
- Clarity of the explanation of the initial project concept.
- Realism and coherence of the objectives defined at the start of the project.
- Explanation of the main engineering decisions taken during design and manufacturing.
- Identification and justification of relevant changes or deviations during the development process.
- Overall clarity and quality of the explanation.
2) Innovation project (maximum 35 points)
- Justification of the selected system or component to be improved.
- Clarity in explaining the expected improvement and the objectives of the innovation.
- Explanation of the development process and decisions taken during the project.
- Demonstration of the innovation implemented in the prototype.
- Technical understanding and mastery of the subject by the presenting students.', 'process', 'recommended', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', true, '[{"op": "max", "value": 25.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 35.0, "unit": "points"}]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.5.4', 'F.9.5.4', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Evaluation and scoring', 'DOCS', 'These values represent the approximate weight of each dimension but do not imply that the presentation will be evaluated strictly by sections.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.9.5.5', 'F.9.5.5', 'F', 9, 'Ms1 7Th Milestone, Final Event Presentation', 'Evaluation and scoring', 'DOCS', 'The jury will assign a global score based on the overall quality of the presentation, the technical understanding demonstrated by the team and the clarity of communication.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MS1-7', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.10.1.1', 'F.10.1.1', 'F', 10, 'Motostudent Electric Deliveries', 'MSE 1st Delivery: Electric and battery pack scheme', 'DOCS', 'The objective of this milestone is to review the electrical architecture and the battery pack concept of the prototypes participating in the MotoStudent Electric category. This delivery must allow the Organization to understand the general design of the electrical system and verify its compliance with the regulation before the Final Event.', 'process', 'required', 'ms1', 'MSE-1', true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.10.1.2', 'F.10.1.2', 'F', 10, 'Motostudent Electric Deliveries', 'MSE 1st Delivery: Electric and battery pack scheme', 'DOCS', 'The submission must include at least the following elements:
- A general unifilar type schematic in order to clearly represent the electrical architecture and connections of the prototype.
- The complete wiring scheme of the prototype.
- The complete wiring harness schematics
- A general description of the battery pack architecture.
- A 3D representation of the battery pack containers or housing.
- The type of cells used and their main technical characteristics.
- The mechanical protection systems implemented for the battery pack and cells.
- A list of the main electrical components of the battery pack and the vehicle, including their name and location within the prototype. Datasheets are not required unless specifically requested by the Organization.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', 'MSE-1', true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.10.1.3', 'F.10.1.3', 'F', 10, 'Motostudent Electric Deliveries', 'MSE 1st Delivery: Electric and battery pack scheme', 'DOCS', 'The Organization reserves the right to request additional information or propose modifications if the submitted design does not clearly demonstrate compliance with the regulation or presents potential safety concerns.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MSE-1', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.10.1.4', 'F.10.1.4', 'F', 10, 'Motostudent Electric Deliveries', 'MSE 1st Delivery: Electric and battery pack scheme', 'DOCS', 'The Organization will provide feedback to the teams within 90 calendar days after the submission deadline.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MSE-1', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.10.2.1', 'F.10.2.1', 'F', 10, 'Motostudent Electric Deliveries', 'MSE 2nd Delivery: Electrical precheck', 'DOCS', 'The objective of this milestone is to perform a preliminary verification of the electrical compliance of the prototype before the Final Event and the official scrutineering process.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MSE-1', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.10.2.2', 'F.10.2.2', 'F', 10, 'Motostudent Electric Deliveries', 'MSE 2nd Delivery: Electrical precheck', 'DOCS', 'The submission must review the relevant requirements described in Section D of this regulation and demonstrate their compliance.', 'process', 'required', 'ms1', 'MSE-1', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.10.2.3', 'F.10.2.3', 'F', 10, 'Motostudent Electric Deliveries', 'MSE 2nd Delivery: Electrical precheck', 'DOCS', 'Teams must include graphical evidence of the implemented solutions whenever possible (for example photographs, diagrams or screenshots).', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', 'MSE-1', true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.10.2.4', 'F.10.2.4', 'F', 10, 'Motostudent Electric Deliveries', 'MSE 2nd Delivery: Electrical precheck', 'DOCS', 'The Organization reserves the right to request additional information or corrections if the provided documentation is insufficient to verify compliance. The Organization will provide feedback to the teams within 90 calendar days after the submission deadline.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'MSE-1', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.11.1.1', 'F.11.1.1', 'F', 11, 'Rider Eligibility Declaration', 'Rider Eligibility Declaration', 'DOCS', 'Each team must submit the rider declaration available on the MotoStudent Platform.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', 'RED', true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.11.1.2', 'F.11.1.2', 'F', 11, 'Rider Eligibility Declaration', 'Rider Eligibility Declaration', 'DOCS', 'Each declared rider must include their riding experience and background.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', 'RED', true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.11.1.3', 'F.11.1.3', 'F', 11, 'Rider Eligibility Declaration', 'Rider Eligibility Declaration', 'DOCS', 'The rider information must comply with the requirements defined in Article G.2. If a team selects or works with a rider prior to the formal declaration period, it shall be the team’s responsibility to verify in advance that such rider is expected to comply with the eligibility requirements defined in these Rules & Regulations.', 'process', 'required', 'ms1', 'RED', true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.11.1.4', 'F.11.1.4', 'F', 11, 'Rider Eligibility Declaration', 'Rider Eligibility Declaration', 'DOCS', 'If the documentation is incomplete or inconsistent, the Organization may request additional information.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', 'RED', false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.1.1', 'F.12.1.1', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Objectives and procedure', 'DOCS', 'The MS2 dynamic tests consist of a series of exercises designed to demonstrate and evaluate the behaviour, performance and reliability of the prototypes developed during the MotoStudent International Competition.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.1.2', 'F.12.1.2', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Objectives and procedure', 'DOCS', 'Each category will have its own independent classification and will compete in parallel during the Final Event.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.1.3', 'F.12.1.3', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Objectives and procedure', 'DOCS', 'All dynamic tests must be carried out by the rider declared by the team during the Administrative Milestone.', 'process', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.1.4', 'F.12.1.4', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Objectives and procedure', 'DOCS', 'Minor adjustments to dimensions, schedules or operational aspects of the tests may be introduced by the Organization during the Final Event if required for safety or operational reasons.', 'process', 'recommended', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.1.5', 'F.12.1.5', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Objectives and procedure', 'DOCS', 'The dynamic tests are designed to evaluate the overall engineering performance of the prototype. The objective is not only to reward the fastest vehicle, but the most balanced and well-developed prototype across multiple performance dimensions such as braking capability, acceleration, agility, consistency and race performance. Teams are therefore encouraged to develop a complete and reliable prototype rather than optimizing the vehicle exclusively for a single test.', 'process', 'recommended', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.1.6', 'F.12.1.6', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Objectives and procedure', 'DOCS', 'All measurements used for scoring purposes will be those recorded by the Organization’s official timing and measurement systems. Data recorded by teams through their own devices (such as GPS loggers, telemetry systems or onboard instrumentation) may differ due to measurement methodology and will not be considered valid for the official competition results.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.1.7', 'F.12.1.7', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Objectives and procedure', 'DOCS', 'Tests 1, 2 and 3 may have two attempts. In such case, the best result obtained by the team will be considered as the valid result for scoring purposes.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.1.8', 'F.12.1.8', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Objectives and procedure', 'DOCS', 'The Competition Organization will publish the official results of each dynamic test as soon as reasonably possible, taking into account the operational needs of the Final Event and any verification or incident review that may be required before validation of the results.', 'process', 'recommended', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.1', 'F.12.2.1', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'The brake test evaluates the distance required for the prototype to come to a complete stop from a minimum speed of 80 km/h.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.2', 'F.12.2.2', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'The start will be given by a signal from a sport marshal at the starting point.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.3', 'F.12.2.3', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'The rider will have a maximum time of 10 seconds from the signal to start the test.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.4', 'F.12.2.4', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'The total length of the acceleration straight is 200 m.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.5', 'F.12.2.5', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'The speed reached at the end of the acceleration straight will be measured by the Competition Organization.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.6', 'F.12.2.6', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'The braking distance will be measured from the speed trap to the foremost part of the prototype once the motorcycle has come to a complete stop.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.7', 'F.12.2.7', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'If the speed measured by the Organization is lower than the required minimum speed, the following penalties will be applied to the measured braking distance:
- < 80.00 km/h and ≥ 79.00 km/h: +4 m
- < 79.00 km/h and ≥ 78.00 km/h: +6 m
- < 78.00 km/h and ≥ 77.00 km/h: +8 m
- < 77.00 km/h and ≥ 76.00 km/h: +10 m
- < 76.00 km/h and ≥ 75.00 km/h: +12 m
- < 75.00 km/h and ≥ 70.00 km/h: +20 m', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.8', 'F.12.2.8', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'If the speed measured is lower than 70.00 km/h the result of the test will be considered as NC (Not Compliant).', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.9', 'F.12.2.9', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'Two photocells will be placed before the braking zone, separated by 1 meter, in order to record the speed during the test.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.10', 'F.12.2.10', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'Graphic description of the test (for illustrative purposes only): Picture 45 - Graphic description of MS1 Test 1: Brake', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.2.11', 'F.12.2.11', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 1: Brake', 'DOCS', 'The score of the test will be assigned according to the ranking of the braking distances obtained (including any applicable penalties), from the lowest distance to the highest. The points will be awarded according to the following table. Rank Score Rank Score Rank Score 1st 90 18th 43 35th 26 2nd 85 19th 42 36th 25 3rd 80 20th 41 37th 24 4th 76 21st 40 38th 23 5th 72 22nd 39 39th 22 6th 68 23rd 38 40th 21 7th 65 24th 37 41st 20 8th 62 25th 36 42nd 19 9th 59 26th 35 43rd 18 10th 56 27th 34 44th 17 11th 54 28th 33 45th 16 12th 52 29th 32 46th 15 13th 50 30th 31 47th 14 14th 48 31st 30 48th 13 15th 46 32nd 29 49th 12 16th 45 33rd 28 50th 11 17th 44 34th 27 … 10 Table 2 - MS2 Test 1: Brake scores', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.3.1', 'F.12.3.1', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 2: Gymkhana', 'DOCS', 'The second test consists of a short circuit designed to evaluate the agility, manoeuvrability and acceleration capability of the prototype.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.3.2', 'F.12.3.2', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 2: Gymkhana', 'DOCS', 'The start will be given by a signal from a sport marshal.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.3.3', 'F.12.3.3', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 2: Gymkhana', 'DOCS', 'Two photocells will be placed at the start and finish line in order to measure the total time required to complete the course.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.3.4', 'F.12.3.4', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 2: Gymkhana', 'DOCS', 'The rider will have a maximum time of 10 seconds from the signal to start the test.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.3.5', 'F.12.3.5', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 2: Gymkhana', 'DOCS', 'If a cone is moved or knocked down by the rider or the prototype, a penalty of 5 seconds will be applied for each cone. If more than 5 cones are moved, the test will result as NC.', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.3.6', 'F.12.3.6', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 2: Gymkhana', 'DOCS', 'If a cone is passed on the wrong side, a penalty of 10 seconds will be applied. If more than 3 cones are incorrectly passed, the test will result as NC.', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.3.7', 'F.12.3.7', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 2: Gymkhana', 'DOCS', 'Graphic description of the test (for illustrative purposes only) (TBC): Picture 46 - Graphical description of MS2 Test 2: Gymkhana. Measures indicated in meters (m)', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.3.8', 'F.12.3.8', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 2: Gymkhana', 'DOCS', 'The score of the test will be assigned according to the ranking of the final times obtained, including any applicable penalties, from the lowest time to the highest. Points will be awarded according to the following table. Rank Score Rank Score Rank Score 1st 70 18th 37 35th 20 2nd 66 19th 36 36th 19 3rd 62 20th 35 37th 18 4th 59 21st 34 38th 17 5th 56 22nd 33 39th 16 6th 53 23rd 32 40th 15 7th 51 24th 31 41st 14 8th 49 25th 30 42nd 13 9th 47 26th 29 43rd 12 10th 45 27th 28 44th 11 11th 44 28th 27 45th 10 12th 43 29th 26 46th 9 13th 42 30th 25 47th 8 14th 41 31st 24 48th 7 15th 40 32nd 23 49th 6 16th 39 33rd 22 50th 5 17th 38 34th 21 … 5 Table 3 - MS2 Test 2: Gymkhana scores', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.4.1', 'F.12.4.1', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 3: Acceleration', 'DOCS', 'The third test consists of a straight-line acceleration run over a distance of 150 m in order to evaluate the acceleration performance of the prototype.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.4.2', 'F.12.4.2', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 3: Acceleration', 'DOCS', 'The start will be given by a signal from a sport marshal at the starting point.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.4.3', 'F.12.4.3', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 3: Acceleration', 'DOCS', 'Two photocells will be placed at the start and at the end of the 150 m straight in order to record the start and end time for each prototype. The difference between both measurements will determine the total time used to evaluate the acceleration performance.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.4.4', 'F.12.4.4', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 3: Acceleration', 'DOCS', 'The rider will have a maximum time of 10 seconds from the signal to start the test.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.4.5', 'F.12.4.5', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 3: Acceleration', 'DOCS', 'Graphic description of the test (for illustrative purposes only): Picture 47 - Graphical description of MS2 Test 3: Acceleration', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.4.6', 'F.12.4.6', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 3: Acceleration', 'DOCS', 'The score of the test will be assigned according to the ranking of the times obtained during the test, from the lowest time to the highest. Points will be awarded according to the following table. Rank Score Rank Score Rank Score 1st 90 18th 43 35th 26 2nd 85 19th 42 36th 25 3rd 80 20th 41 37th 24 4th 76 21st 40 38th 23 5th 72 22nd 39 39th 22 6th 68 23rd 38 40th 21 7th 65 24th 37 41st 20 8th 62 25th 36 42nd 19 9th 59 26th 35 43rd 18 10th 56 27th 34 44th 17 11th 54 28th 33 45th 16 12th 52 29th 32 46th 15 13th 50 30th 31 47th 14 14th 48 31st 30 48th 13 15th 46 32nd 29 49th 12 16th 45 33rd 28 50th 11 17th 44 34th 27 … 10 Table 4 - MS2 Test 3: Acceleration test score Rank Score', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.5.1', 'F.12.5.1', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 4: Vmax', 'DOCS', 'This test consists of recording the maximum speed reached at the official speed trap during the Free Practice 2 session.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.5.2', 'F.12.5.2', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 4: Vmax', 'DOCS', 'Any valid passage through the speed trap (including laps without passing through the finish line), respecting track limits, will be considered for the test.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.5.3', 'F.12.5.3', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 4: Vmax', 'DOCS', 'The highest recorded speed for each team will be used to determine the classification.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.5.4', 'F.12.5.4', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 4: Vmax', 'DOCS', 'The score of the test will be assigned according to the ranking of the maximum speeds recorded for each team, from the highest speed to the lowest. Points will be awarded according to the following table. Rank Score Rank Score Rank Score 1st 30 18th 10 35th 7 2nd 27 19th 10 36th 6 3rd 25 20th 10 37th 6 4th 23 21st 9 38th 6 5th 22 22nd 9 39th 6 6th 21 23rd 9 40th 6 7th 20 24th 9 41st 5 8th 19 25th 9 42nd 5 9th 18 26th 8 43rd 5 10th 17 27th 8 44th 5 11th 16 28th 8 45th 5 12th 15 29th 8 46th 4 13th 14 30th 8 47th 4 14th 13 31st 7 48th 4 15th 12 32nd 7 49th 4 16th 11 33rd 7 50th 4 17th 10 34th 7 … 3 Table 5 - MS2 Test 4: Vmax scores', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.6.1', 'F.12.6.1', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 5: Regularity', 'DOCS', 'The regularity test evaluates the consistency of the prototype and rider combination. The objective of this test is to determine the consistency of the lap times achieved in Sector 2 of the Speed Circuit during the Warm-up session.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.6.2', 'F.12.6.2', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 5: Regularity', 'DOCS', 'All Sector 2 times recorded during the test will be considered for the evaluation, including laps that do not complete the full lap, provided that track limits are respected.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.6.3', 'F.12.6.3', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 5: Regularity', 'DOCS', 'For each team, the regularity value will be calculated using the Sector 2 times recorded during the session. The recorded sector times will be sorted in ascending order and the minimum difference between the nth and the (n+2)th sector times will be determined, where n ranges from 1 to m−2 and m represents the total number of recorded sector times. min (|𝑥𝑛 − 𝑥𝑛+2 |)', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.6.4', 'F.12.6.4', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 5: Regularity', 'DOCS', 'The score of the test will be assigned according to the ranking of the regularity values obtained by each team, from the lowest time difference to the highest. Points will be awarded according to the following table. Rank Score Rank Score Rank Score 1st 50 18th 23 35th 9 2nd 46 19th 22 36th 8 3rd 43 20th 21 37th 8 4th 40 21st 20 38th 8 5th 38 22nd 19 39th 8 6th 36 23rd 18 40th 8 7th 34 24th 17 41st 7 8th 33 25th 16 42nd 7 9th 32 26th 15 43rd 7 10th 31 27th 14 44th 7 11th 30 28th 13 45th 7 12th 29 29th 12 46th 6 13th 28 30th 11 47th 6 14th 27 31st 10 48th 6 15th 26 32nd 9 49th 6 16th 25 33rd 9 50th 6 17th 24 34th 9 … 5 Table 6 - MS2 Test 5: Regularity scores', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.7.1', 'F.12.7.1', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 6: Pole position', 'DOCS', 'This test corresponds to the fastest lap time obtained during the official Qualifying session.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.7.2', 'F.12.7.2', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 6: Pole position', 'DOCS', 'The score of the test will be assigned according to the ranking of the lap times recorded during the Qualifying session, from the lowest time to the highest. Points will be awarded according to the following table. Rank Score Rank Score Rank Score 1st 30 18th 10 35th 7 2nd 27 19th 10 36th 6 3rd 25 20th 10 37th 6 4th 23 21st 9 38th 6 5th 22 22nd 9 39th 6 6th 21 23rd 9 40th 6 7th 20 24th 9 41st 5 8th 19 25th 9 42nd 5 9th 18 26th 8 43rd 5 10th 17 27th 8 44th 5 11th 16 28th 8 45th 5 12th 15 29th 8 46th 4 13th 14 30th 8 47th 4 14th 13 31st 7 48th 4 15th 12 32nd 7 49th 4 16th 11 33rd 7 50th 4 17th 10 34th 7 … 3 Table 7 - MS2 Test 6: Pole position scores', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.8.1', 'F.12.8.1', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 7: Best Race Lap', 'DOCS', 'This test corresponds to the fastest lap time achieved during the Play-Off race and / or the Final race.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.8.2', 'F.12.8.2', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 7: Best Race Lap', 'DOCS', 'For teams participating in both races, only the fastest lap obtained in the Final race will be considered.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.8.3', 'F.12.8.3', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 7: Best Race Lap', 'DOCS', 'The score of the test will be assigned according to the ranking of the best lap times recorded during the race sessions, from the lowest time to the highest. Points will be awarded according to the following table. Rank Score Rank Score Rank Score 1st 30 16th 11 31st 7 2nd 27 17th 10 32nd 7 3rd 25 18th 10 33rd 7 4th 23 19th 10 34th 7 5th 22 20th 10 35th 7 6th 21 21st 9 36th 6 7th 20 22nd 9 37th 6 8th 19 23rd 9 38th 6 9th 18 24th 9 39th 6 10th 17 25th 9 40th 6 11th 16 26th 8 41st 5 12th 15 27th 8 42nd 5 13th 14 28th 8 43rd 5 14th 13 29th 8 44th 5 15th 12 30th 8 … 5 Table 8 - MS2 Test 7: Best Race Lap scores', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.9.1', 'F.12.9.1', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 8: Race result', 'DOCS', 'The result of Test 8: Race Result will be determined according to the official classification of the Final Race and the Play-Off Race. For the purposes of Test 8 scoring, teams classified in the Final Race shall be ranked first, followed by teams classified in the Play-Off Race. Teams not classified in either race, including DNFs, shall be ranked after all classified teams and ordered according to the distance completed in their respective race.', 'process', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.12.9.2', 'F.12.9.2', 'F', 12, 'Ms2 Phase', 'Test 8: Race result', 'DOCS', 'The score of the test will be assigned according to the ranking defined in Art. F.12.9.1, from the highest finishing position to the lowest. Points will be awarded according to the following table. Rank Score Rank Score Rank Score 1st 150 16th 75 31st 43 2nd 143 17th 72 32nd 42 3rd 136 18th 69 33rd 41 4th 130 19th 66 34th 40 5th 124 20th 63 35th 39 6th 118 21st 60 36th 38 7th 113 22nd 58 37th 37 8th 108 23rd 56 38th 36 9th 103 24th 54 39th 35 10th 98 25th 52 40th 34 11th 94 26th 50 41st 33 12th 90 27th 48 42nd 32 13th 86 28th 46 43rd 31 14th 82 29th 45 44th 30 15th 78 30th 44 … 0 Table 9 - MS2 Test 8: Race result scores', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.1.1', 'F.13.1.1', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'General Principles', 'DOCS', 'The MotoStudent Awards recognise the teams that demonstrate excellence in project development, technical performance and sporting results throughout the MotoStudent International Competition.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.2.1', 'F.13.2.1', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS1 Awards', 'DOCS', 'The Best MS1 Award is granted to the team from each category that achieves the highest MS1 score (maximum of 600 points), calculated as the sum of the following milestones minus any applicable penalties:
- MS1 1st milestone: Team plan (maximum of 75 points)
- MS1 2nd milestone: Product definition (maximum of 100 points)
- MS1 3rd milestone: Innovation (maximum of 150 points)
- MS1 4th milestone: Prototype CAD and Drawings (maximum of 60 points)
- MS1 5th milestone: Economical Plan (maximum of 75 points)
- MS1 6th milestone: Pitch Presentation (maximum of 80 points)
- MS1 7th milestone: Final Event Presentation (maximum of 60 points)', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[{"op": "max", "value": 600.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 75.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 100.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 150.0, "unit": "points"}]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.2.2', 'F.13.2.2', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS1 Awards', 'DOCS', 'The Best Design Award recognises the team that achieves the highest score (maximum of 220 points) considering the following milestones minus any applicable penalties:
- MS1 2nd milestone: Product Definition (maximum of 100 points)
- MS1 4th milestone: Prototype CAD and Drawings (maximum of 60 points)
- MS1 7th milestone: Final Event Presentation (maximum of 60 points)', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[{"op": "max", "value": 220.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 100.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 60.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 60.0, "unit": "points"}]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.2.3', 'F.13.2.3', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS1 Awards', 'DOCS', 'The Best Innovation Award recognises the team that achieves the highest score (maximum of 210 points) considering the following milestones minus any applicable penalties:
- MS1 3rd milestone: Innovation (maximum of 150 points)
- MS1 7th milestone: Final Event presentation (maximum of 60 points)', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[{"op": "max", "value": 210.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 150.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 60.0, "unit": "points"}]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.2.4', 'F.13.2.4', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS1 Awards', 'DOCS', 'In case of a tie in any MS1 award, the Organization will apply a justified tie-breaker methodology.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.2.5', 'F.13.2.5', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS1 Awards', 'DOCS', 'Tie-breakers apply only to determine the awarded team and do not modify the official classification.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.2.6', 'F.13.2.6', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS1 Awards', 'DOCS', 'For clarity and reference, the following table summarizes the MS1 awards and the milestones contributing to each award: Milestones MS1 Awards 1st 2nd 3rd 4th 5th 6th 7th Best MS1 Best Design (out of 220 points) 100 60 60 (out of 600 Best Innovation (out of 210 points) 150 points) 75 75 80 Table 10 - MS1 Awards', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.3.1', 'F.13.3.1', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS2 Awards', 'DOCS', 'The total MS2 score (maximum of 540 points) is obtained by adding the scores achieved in the following dynamic tests:
- Test 1: Brake (maximum of 90 points)
- Test 2: Gymkhana (maximum of 70 points)
- Test 3: Acceleration (maximum of 90 points)
- Test 4: Vmax (maximum of 30 points)
- Test 5: Regularity (maximum of 50 points)
- Test 6: Pole Position (maximum of 30 points)
- Test 7: Best Race Lap (maximum of 30 points)
- Test 8: Race Result (maximum of 150 points)', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, true, '[{"op": "max", "value": 540.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 90.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 70.0, "unit": "points"}, {"op": "max", "value": 90.0, "unit": "points"}]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.3.2', 'F.13.3.2', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS2 Awards', 'DOCS', 'The Best MS2 Award is granted to the teams finishing in 1st, 2nd and 3rd position in the MS2 classification for each category.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.3.3', 'F.13.3.3', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS2 Awards', 'DOCS', 'If, for reasons beyond the Organization’s control, one or more scoring tests must be cancelled, the Competition Organization reserves the right to adjust the allocation of points for the affected tests, with prior notification to the participating teams.', 'process', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.3.4', 'F.13.3.4', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS2 Awards', 'DOCS', 'In case of a tie in the MS2 classification, the following criterion will be applied until the tie is resolved:
- Best MS1 Award score', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.3.5', 'F.13.3.5', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'MS2 Awards', 'DOCS', 'Tie-breakers apply only to determine the awarded teams and do not modify the official classification.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.4.1', 'F.13.4.1', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'Overall Category Awards', 'DOCS', 'The Best MotoStudent Award is granted to the team from each category that achieves the highest overall score, obtained by summing the following scores and applying any applicable penalties:
- Best MS1 Award score.
- Best MS2 Award score.', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.4.2', 'F.13.4.2', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'Overall Category Awards', 'DOCS', 'The Best Rookie Award is granted to the rookie team (representing a campus not previously registered in that MotoStudent category) that achieves the highest overall score, calculated as the sum of the following scores minus any applicable penalties:
- Best MS1 Award score.
- Best MS2 Award score.', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.4.3', 'F.13.4.3', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'Overall Category Awards', 'DOCS', 'In case of a tie for the Best MotoStudent or Best Rookie awards, the deciding criterion will be:
- Best MS1 Award score If the tie persists, the jury will determine the awarded team. Tie-breakers apply only to determine the awarded team and do not modify the official classification.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.5.1', 'F.13.5.1', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'Special Nominations', 'DOCS', 'The MotoStudent Fair Play nomination highlights the team that best represents the values of respect, integrity, teamwork, and professional conduct throughout all phases of the competition. This recognition has a special character, as it will be voted on by the participating teams themselves, who will be able to select the team they believe has demonstrated exemplary behaviour both on and off the track. The winning team will be the one that receives the highest number of nominations through a quiz available on the MotoStudent platform, which will be open from the first to the last day of the Final Event. In this way, the teams themselves will recognize those participants who best represent the spirit of the competition. This recognition does not affect the scoring or the official ranking of the competition. In the event of a tie, the Organization will apply the tie-breaking criteria it considers appropriate.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.5.2', 'F.13.5.2', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'Special Nominations', 'DOCS', 'The MotoStudent Media Hero nomination aims to recognize the team that stands out the most in communicating, promoting and increasing the visibility of its project throughout the Competition. As MotoStudent teams are multidisciplinary, this nomination also seeks to highlight the work carried out in areas such as communication, marketing, and project management visibility, which play a key role in enhancing the team’s outreach and visibility. This is a recognition-based nomination, and therefore it does not impact the official scoring or final ranking of the Competition. It shall be awarded to the team that stands out the most in terms of visibility and communication, based on an overall evaluation carried out by a designated jury. The evaluation is based on the team’s overall performance throughout the entire competition. In this regard, the following aspects will be considered:
- Consistency and level of activity across communication channels, digital platforms, and social media (especially Instagram).
- The quality, creativity, and relevance of the content produced.
- The ability to communicate clearly and effectively both the project’s development and the team’s identity.
- The coherence, planning, and evolution of the communication strategy throughout the competition.
- Proactivity in promoting the project through the organization or participation in fairs, events, collaborations, promotional actions, or activities within the university environment.
- The development of initiatives aimed at increasing the visibility of the team and its project, regardless of their scale, format, or reach.
- Participation in initiatives promoted by the MotoStudent organization, such as the Poster Contest, campaigns, prototype presentations or similar activities. Teams are encouraged to create and publish audiovisual content throughout the Competition that reflects the evolution of their project, such as team presentation videos, prototype development updates, innovation-related content or other materials of similar nature. Although such audiovisual content is not a mandatory deliverable, its development and publication may be positively considered in the evaluation of this nomination, as it constitutes one of the most effective ways to communicate the evolution, identity and visibility of the project over time. The absence of audiovisual content does not automatically exclude a team from this nomination, but it may significantly reduce the team’s ability to demonstrate sustained communication effort and project visibility throughout the Competition. Furthermore, this content may serve as a foundation for the preparation of the MS1 6th Milestone, Pitch Presentation, helping teams deliver a more complete and structured presentation of their project. Through this nomination, MotoStudent aims to encourage teams to actively share their work, connect with the public, and strengthen the visibility of their project beyond the technical field.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.6.1', 'F.13.6.1', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'General Provisions', 'DOCS', 'The economic or material value of each award will be communicated by the Organization to all registered teams.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.6.2', 'F.13.6.2', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'General Provisions', 'DOCS', 'Awards cannot be shared or transferred to another team.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.6.3', 'F.13.6.3', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'General Provisions', 'DOCS', 'The Organization reserves the right to introduce additional awards during the development of the MotoStudent International Competition.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.13.6.4', 'F.13.6.4', 'F', 13, 'Motostudent Awards', 'General Provisions', 'DOCS', 'If a test is declared null or cancelled, the Organization reserves the right to define a new scoring distribution for that test.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.1.1', 'F.14.1.1', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'General submission requirements', 'DOCS', 'All deliverables must be submitted in digital format via the MotoStudent Platform, except for the Final Event Presentation.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.1.2', 'F.14.1.2', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'General submission requirements', 'DOCS', 'The main document of each deliverable must be submitted in PDF format. All relevant information required for the evaluation must be included in the main PDF document. Supporting files are considered complementary and may not be reviewed by the jury.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.1.3', 'F.14.1.3', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'General submission requirements', 'DOCS', 'Additional supporting files (e.g. CAD models, datasets or technical drawings) may be submitted only when they are relevant to the deliverable and must be provided in commonly accepted engineering formats.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.1.4', 'F.14.1.4', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'General submission requirements', 'DOCS', 'All submitted files must be properly optimized and compressed to ensure efficient upload, storage and review. Teams are responsible for minimizing file sizes without compromising the clarity and quality of the information. The Organization reserves the right not to accept or not to consider files that are excessively large, not properly optimized, or not clearly required for the evaluation of the deliverable.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.1.5', 'F.14.1.5', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'General submission requirements', 'DOCS', 'Each deliverable must be prepared and submitted by registered Team Members. If a deliverable is submitted by a person not registered as an official Team Member, the delivery score will result in NC.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.1.6', 'F.14.1.6', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'General submission requirements', 'DOCS', 'Deliverables must be submitted in one of the official competition languages. Otherwise, the delivery score will result in NC.', 'process', 'required', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.1.7', 'F.14.1.7', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'General submission requirements', 'DOCS', 'Once a deliverable has been submitted, it cannot be modified, replaced or resubmitted unless expressly authorized by the Organization.', 'deliverable', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.1.8', 'F.14.1.8', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'General submission requirements', 'DOCS', 'Teams are responsible for ensuring that the submission is correctly completed. Technical issues, upload errors or incorrect submissions will not justify resubmission unless expressly accepted by the Organization.', 'process', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.2.1', 'F.14.2.1', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Deliverable format requirements', 'DOCS', 'Each deliverable must include a cover and an index page.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.2.2', 'F.14.2.2', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Deliverable format requirements', 'DOCS', 'All pages must be numbered, except the cover and index pages, which may not display the page number but shall count towards the total page limit.', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.2.3', 'F.14.2.3', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Deliverable format requirements', 'DOCS', 'The maximum length of each deliverable is 50 pages, including cover, index, figures, tables and references. Any content exceeding the page limit will not be considered during evaluation.', 'deliverable', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.2.4', 'F.14.2.4', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Deliverable format requirements', 'DOCS', 'Only DIN A4 page format is allowed, except for tables and graphs, which may be presented in DIN A3 format. Each DIN A3 page may only contain a single table or a single graph and its corresponding title.', 'deliverable', 'recommended', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.2.5', 'F.14.2.5', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Deliverable format requirements', 'DOCS', 'The format must comply with the following:
- Margins:
- Left: 3 cm
- Right: 3 cm
- Top: 2.5 cm
- Bottom: 2.5 cm
- Line spacing: 1.5
- Paragraph spacing:
- Before: 0 pt
- After: 6 pt
- Font:
- Type: Arial
- Size: 11 (except titles, subtitles and tables)', 'deliverable', 'required', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.2.6', 'F.14.2.6', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Deliverable format requirements', 'DOCS', 'No annexes or additional documentation may be included unless explicitly required by these Rules & Regulations.', 'process', 'recommended', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.3.1', 'F.14.3.1', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Penalties applicable to MS1 deliverables', 'DOCS', 'Failure to comply with any applicable technical regulation defined in Sections B, C or D will result in a NC score.', 'process', 'blocking', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.3.2', 'F.14.3.2', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Penalties applicable to MS1 deliverables', 'DOCS', 'If a deliverable does not include a cover or index page, or does not comply with the required format, the delivery score will be penalized with a MP.', 'deliverable', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.3.3', 'F.14.3.3', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Penalties applicable to MS1 deliverables', 'DOCS', 'Submission of a deliverable within 10 days after the deadline (240 hours) will result in a MP in that delivery score.', 'deliverable', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.3.4', 'F.14.3.4', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Penalties applicable to MS1 deliverables', 'DOCS', 'Deliverables submitted more than 10 days after the deadline (240 hours) may not be accepted by the Organization and will result in a NP.', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.3.5', 'F.14.3.5', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'Penalties applicable to MS1 deliverables', 'DOCS', 'The minimum possible score of a deliverable is 0 points.', 'deliverable', 'info', 'ms1', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.4.1', 'F.14.4.1', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'MotoStudent Electric deliverables specific penalties', 'DOCS', 'Submission of any documentation within 10 days after its deadline (240 hours later) will result in a Minor Penalty (MP) applied to the total MS1 score.', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.4.2', 'F.14.4.2', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'MotoStudent Electric deliverables specific penalties', 'DOCS', 'Failure to submit or submission later than 10 days after the deadline (240 hours later) will result in a Severe Penalty (SP) applied to the total MS1 score. In this case, the team must inform the Organization via ticket in order to review the delivery.', 'deliverable', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.4.3', 'F.14.4.3', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'MotoStudent Electric deliverables specific penalties', 'DOCS', 'The Organization reserves the right not to accept any delivery submitted more than 10 days after the deadline (240 hours later), resulting in a Not Presented (NP).', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('F.14.4.4', 'F.14.4.4', 'F', 14, 'Deliverable Submissions And Penalties', 'MotoStudent Electric deliverables specific penalties', 'DOCS', 'In case of a NP score in any of the MSE deliveries before the Final Event, the team shall contact the Organization. The Organization reserves the right not to scrutineer any bike that has a NP score in any MSE delivery. SECTI ON G: SP ORTI NG RE GULATI ONS FOR MS2 P HASE SECTION G SPORTING REGULATIONS FOR MS2 PHASE', 'process', 'penalty', 'ms1', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.1.1.1', 'G.1.1.1', 'G', 1, 'Goals And Conditions', 'MS2 definition', 'RACEOP', 'The MS2 Phase consists of a series of dynamic tests aimed at evaluating the performance and behaviour of the manufactured prototype.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.1.2.1', 'G.1.2.1', 'G', 1, 'Goals And Conditions', 'Requirements', 'RACEOP', 'In order to participate in the MS2 Phase, teams must comply with the requirements defined in this section.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.1.2.2', 'G.1.2.2', 'G', 1, 'Goals And Conditions', 'Requirements', 'RACEOP', 'Only prototypes that have successfully passed the Scrutineering process (Section E) are allowed to participate in the MS2 Phase. Prototypes must be presented in safe and suitable conditions to take part in the dynamic tests. The Organization Technical Staff may inspect the condition of the prototype at any time during the Final Event.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.1.3.1', 'G.1.3.1', 'G', 1, 'Goals And Conditions', 'MS2 Sports Committee', 'RACEOP', 'The MS2 Phase will be supervised and managed by the MS2 Sports Committee, which will include at least the following officials:
- Competition General Manager
- Competition Sport Director
- Race Director
- Race Director Assistant
- Sporting Jury (Officials’ coordinators)
- Timekeeping Director
- Competition Technical Director
- Chief Scrutineer', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.1.1', 'G.2.1.1', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Definition', 'RACEOP', 'Each team must nominate one rider responsible for riding the prototype during the MS2 Phase tests. As MotoStudent aims to evaluate the engineering work and the prototype performance rather than the rider ability, specific eligibility restrictions are applied to ensure fair conditions among teams.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.2.1', 'G.2.2.1', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Eligibility', 'RACEOP', 'Once approved by the Competition Organization, the rider shall be officially registered with the team exclusively for the purpose of riding the prototype during the MS2 Phase and the Final Event. The rider shall be registered through the submission of the Rider Eligibility Declaration. Riders are not required to be registered as Team Members through the MotoStudent Platform. The rider may access the areas and activities strictly necessary to perform the riding duties during the Final Event and must comply with all rules, safety instructions and obligations applicable to participants. The rider is not considered a Team Member and therefore shall not take part in the design, development, modification, repair or technical work on the prototype, unless the rider is simultaneously registered as a Team Member in accordance with the applicable requirements. Riders are also exempt from the academic eligibility requirements applicable to Team Members.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.2.2', 'G.2.2.2', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Eligibility', 'RACEOP', 'The rider is not required to pay any entry fee to participate in the Competition.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.2.3', 'G.2.2.3', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Eligibility', 'RACEOP', 'The rider must be at least 18 years old on the first day of the Final Event.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.2.4', 'G.2.2.4', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Eligibility', 'RACEOP', 'The participation of riders who have competed within the last 10 years prior to the Final Event in Circuit Racing events organized under the authority of FIM, FIM Continental Unions (Europe, Asia, North America, Latin America, Africa, Oceania), or in the highest-level National Circuit Racing Championship officially organized or recognized by the corresponding national motorcycle federation is not allowed. This restriction also applies to riders who have participated in such competitions as Wild Card or replacement riders in one or more events. For the purpose of this regulation, the highest-level National Circuit Racing Championships includes the highest-level circuit racing championships organized and designated by national motorcycle federations. In case of doubt regarding the eligibility of a rider or the status of a specific championship, the Organization reserves the right to determine whether the competition is considered a high-level National Championship for the purposes of this regulation. Participation in previous editions of MotoStudent is exempt from this restriction.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.2.5', 'G.2.2.5', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Eligibility', 'RACEOP', 'A student may hold a federation license and participate as a rider. However, if the rider is not registered as an official Team Member, he/she will only be allowed to ride the prototype.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.2.6', 'G.2.2.6', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Eligibility', 'RACEOP', 'Each rider must be registered with a single team and may only participate with that team in the corresponding category. A rider cannot participate with multiple teams, even if they belong to the same university or compete in different categories.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.2.7', 'G.2.2.7', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Eligibility', 'RACEOP', 'The rider must attend all mandatory briefing sessions organized prior to the MS2 Phase tests and any additional meetings requested by the Organization.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.2.8', 'G.2.2.8', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Eligibility', 'RACEOP', 'If the rider withdraws during the Final Event due to medical reasons or force majeure, no replacement rider will be allowed.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.3.1', 'G.2.3.1', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Federative requirements', 'RACEOP', 'The rider must hold a valid federative license allowing participation in an international FIM competition such as MotoStudent. Track day insurance policies or federation licenses that do not cover participation in FIM international competitions will not be accepted.', 'sporting', 'blocking', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.3.2', 'G.2.3.2', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Federative requirements', 'RACEOP', 'Riders participating in MotoStudent must hold one of the following licenses *:
- RFME:
- RFME homologated license Or
- RFME One Event homologated license
- FIM
- FIM International Racing Meetings Annual license Or
- FIM International Racing Meetings - One Event license Or
- FIM Superbike/Supersport World Championship license Or
- FIM World Endurance Championship license
- Others:
- **For FIM Europe Countries only**: National license + Start Permission. *** These federative requirements may vary depending on the conditions imposed by the motorcycle federations involved (FIM, RFME and FARAM) for the corresponding competition season.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.3.3', 'G.2.3.3', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Federative requirements', 'RACEOP', 'Teams may process temporary licenses for their riders through:
- Aragonese Motorcycling Federation (www.faram.es).
- Royal Spanish Motorcycling Federation (www.rfme.com).', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.4.1', 'G.2.4.1', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Communication with the rider', 'RACEOP', 'Radio communication or any other electronic communication between the team and the rider during the MS2 Phase tests is strictly forbidden.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.4.2', 'G.2.4.2', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Communication with the rider', 'RACEOP', 'Communication between the team and the rider is only allowed through a pit board displayed from the Pit Wall during Free Practice, Warm Up, Qualifying and Race sessions.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.4.3', 'G.2.4.3', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Communication with the rider', 'RACEOP', 'The pit board must be lightweight and must not exceed 1 m in width and 1.5 m in height.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[{"op": "max", "value": 1.0, "unit": "m"}]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.4.4', 'G.2.4.4', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Communication with the rider', 'RACEOP', 'The pit board must be handled by a single Team Member, who must hold it securely to avoid any risk of falling onto the track.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.4.5', 'G.2.4.5', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Communication with the rider', 'RACEOP', 'The pit board may only be shown when the rider passes through the Finish Straight and must immediately be removed afterwards. The board must never be placed on the track surface.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.5.1', 'G.2.5.1', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider replacement', 'RACEOP', 'Any rider replacement must be authorized by the Organization. Typical reasons for a replacement may include:
- Injury of the main rider
- Unavailability of the main rider due to schedule changes affecting the Final Event', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.5.2', 'G.2.5.2', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider replacement', 'RACEOP', 'Rider replacements requested up to one week before the beginning of the Final Event (previous Wednesday not included) will be subject to an administrative fee.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.5.3', 'G.2.5.3', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider replacement', 'RACEOP', 'Rider replacements requested during the week prior to the Final Event (from the previous Wednesday until the administrative checks) will be subject to a double administrative fee.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.5.4', 'G.2.5.4', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider replacement', 'RACEOP', 'Once the rider administrative checks have been completed during the Final Event, rider replacement will not be permitted.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.6.1', 'G.2.6.1', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Medical Fitness', 'RACEOP', 'After any crash, incident or situation that may affect the physical condition of the rider, the Organization may require a medical evaluation before allowing the rider to continue participating in the session or in the Event.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.6.2', 'G.2.6.2', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Medical Fitness', 'RACEOP', 'The Official Medical Service has the authority to declare a rider FIT or UNFIT to continue participating in the Event. Race Direction may prevent a rider from continuing to participate if the rider is considered a safety risk for himself/herself or for other participants.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.2.6.3', 'G.2.6.3', 'G', 2, 'Rider', 'Rider Medical Fitness', 'RACEOP', 'The decision of the Official Medical Service regarding the medical fitness of a rider is final and cannot be appealed.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.1.1', 'G.3.1.1', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Weather conditions', 'RACEOP', 'In case of rain, the Organization may declare two different rain conditions:
- Moderate rain
- Intense rain', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.1.2', 'G.3.1.2', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Weather conditions', 'RACEOP', 'If moderate rain is declared, both MotoStudent eFuel and MotoStudent Electric teams may continue the MS2 Phase tests. The use of wet weather tires may be advisable.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.1.3', 'G.3.1.3', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Weather conditions', 'RACEOP', 'If intense rain is declared, all MS2 Phase tests will be suspended and any prototype outside its Box must return immediately.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.1.4', 'G.3.1.4', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Weather conditions', 'RACEOP', 'In case of intense rain, the Organization will inform the teams whether the affected test is cancelled or postponed.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.1.5', 'G.3.1.5', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Weather conditions', 'RACEOP', 'For any other weather conditions or unforeseen circumstances, the MS2 Sports Committee will decide whether the tests are postponed, modified or cancelled.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.1.6', 'G.3.1.6', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Weather conditions', 'RACEOP', 'The Organization reserves the right to modify the schedule or evaluation procedures due to weather conditions or other unforeseen events.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.2.1', 'G.3.2.1', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Access to the track', 'RACEOP', 'Prototypes must enter the track only through the designated access points established by the Organization for each test.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.3.1', 'G.3.3.1', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour on the track:', 'RACEOP', 'Riding in the opposite direction of the track is strictly forbidden.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.3.2', 'G.3.3.2', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour on the track:', 'RACEOP', 'In the event of an accident or mechanical failure, the rider must immediately move the prototype off-track and off the racing line to a safe area where it does not endanger other riders.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.3.3', 'G.3.3.3', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour on the track:', 'RACEOP', 'No person may approach a stopped prototype on the track except the rider, Race Direction officials, marshals or authorized Technical Staff.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.3.4', 'G.3.3.4', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour on the track:', 'RACEOP', 'In the event of a crash, the rider must move to a safe area as soon as possible. Track marshals will assess the situation and determine whether the rider may safely continue the session. If the prototype is considered unsafe or has suffered significant damage, the marshals may require the prototype to be removed from the track and inspected by the Technical Scrutineers before it is allowed to rejoin any session.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.1', 'G.3.4.1', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'The maximum speed limit in the Pit Lane is 60 km/h.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.2', 'G.3.4.2', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'Only properly accredited personnel are allowed in the Pit Lane. The Organization may remove any person whose presence is not justified.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.3', 'G.3.4.3', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'If oil or any other liquid is spilled in the Pit Lane working area, the prototype may not start until both the prototype and the affected area have been completely cleaned.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.4', 'G.3.4.4', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'For the MotoStudent eFuel category, if the engine automatic starting system does not work, up to two people may assist the rider by pushing the prototype to the Pit Lane exit. External batteries or auxiliary starting devices are not allowed.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.5', 'G.3.4.5', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'If a rider experiences a problem before reaching the Pit Lane exit, the prototype may return to the Box with the engine / motor switched off through the work zone and accompanied by a Pit Lane marshal.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.6', 'G.3.4.6', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'During pit stops only registered members can manipulate the prototype in pit lane. Failure to comply with this rule may result in the exclusion of the team.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.7', 'G.3.4.7', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'During pit stops, only registered Team Members may manipulate the prototype. Failure to comply with this rule may result in the exclusion of the team from the session. A maximum of five (5) people may be in contact with or manipulating the prototype, including the rider. Any physical contact with the prototype will be considered as manipulation for the purpose of this limit, even if the rider remains on the motorcycle without actively intervening.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.8', 'G.3.4.8', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'If work is carried out inside the Box, the number of Team Members working on the prototype is not limited (the rider is not considered as Team Member for this effect). During race sessions, introducing the prototype into the Box may result in exclusion from that session (see Articles G.6.2.1(17) and G.6.2.2(17)).', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.9', 'G.3.4.9', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'Oil or liquid changes and cleaning operations must be performed inside the Box using appropriate containers. Teams must ensure the area remains clean after these operations.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.10', 'G.3.4.10', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'Stopping the prototype in the fast lane of the Pit Lane (between the red line and the Pit Wall) is strictly forbidden.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb)
on conflict (clause_key) do update set
  printed_ref = excluded.printed_ref, section = excluded.section,
  article = excluded.article, article_title = excluded.article_title,
  group_title = excluded.group_title, subteam_key = excluded.subteam_key,
  body = excluded.body, obligation = excluded.obligation,
  criticality = excluded.criticality, phase = excluded.phase,
  milestone_key = excluded.milestone_key,
  is_team_duty = excluded.is_team_duty, specs = excluded.specs;

insert into clauses (clause_key, printed_ref, section, article, article_title, group_title, subteam_key, body, obligation, criticality, phase, milestone_key, is_team_duty, specs) values
  ('G.3.4.11', 'G.3.4.11', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'Smoking, eating, drinking, or using bicycles, electric scooters or any other personal vehicles is forbidden in the Pit Lane.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.4.12', 'G.3.4.12', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Behaviour at the Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'The use of chairs or tables in the Pit Lane is not allowed.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.5.1', 'G.3.5.1', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Flag Signals', 'RACEOP', 'The following flag signals will be used to alert riders during the MS2 Phase tests:
- Red flag: waved at all marshal posts to indicate that the session is stopped.
- Black flag: shown together with the rider’s number. The rider must return to the pits at the end of the current lap.
- Black flag with orange disc: shown together with the rider’s number to indicate a mechanical problem that may endanger the rider or others. The rider must leave the track immediately.
- Yellow flag: indicates danger on or near the track. Riders must slow down and overtaking is forbidden.
- One (1) yellow flag: hazard beside the track.
- Two (2) yellow flags: hazard on the track.
- White flag with red diagonal cross: rain affecting that section of the track.
- Yellow and red striped flag: reduced adhesion on the track surface due to substances other than rain.
- Green flag: track is clear. End of hazard zone and end of overtaking prohibition.
- Blue flag: shown to indicate that a faster rider is approaching and the slower rider must allow safe overtaking.
- Chequered black/white flag: indicates the end of a practice session or race.
- Chequered black/white flag together with blue flag: used when a rider closely follows the leader on the final lap (see Article G.6.4.1).', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.5.2', 'G.3.5.2', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Flag Signals', 'RACEOP', 'Any failure to respect flag signals may be penalized.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.3.6.1', 'G.3.6.1', 'G', 3, 'Sport Behaviour', 'Regulations priority order', 'RACEOP', 'Any situation not covered by the MotoStudent Rules & Regulations will be governed by the current RFME ESBK Sporting Regulations. If the situation is not covered there, the current RFME General Sporting Regulations for Speed Competitions will apply. The current RFME ESBK Sporting Regulations can be consulted at: https://rfme.com/campeonatos/campeonato-de-espana-de-superbike/ The RFME General Sporting Regulations can be consulted at: https://rfme.com/rfme/estatutos-y-codigos-rfme/', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.1.1', 'G.4.1.1', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Practice session track', 'RACEOP', 'Practice sessions will take place on the MotorLand Aragón FIM Grand Prix Circuit layout, with a total length of 5,077.65 m. The circuit layout is shown in Annex 2 of Section J of these Rules & Regulations.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.2.1', 'G.4.2.1', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Development of the sessions', 'RACEOP', 'Riders may enter the track from the pit lane when the green light is displayed at the pit exit.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.2.2', 'G.4.2.2', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Development of the sessions', 'RACEOP', 'The practice session time will start when the pit exit green light is switched on. A visible board or countdown display in the pit lane will indicate the remaining session time.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.2.3', 'G.4.2.3', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Development of the sessions', 'RACEOP', 'The end of the session will be indicated by the chequered flag waved at the finish line, after which the pit exit will be closed. Lap times will continue to be recorded until each rider crosses the finish line after the allotted session time has elapsed. Riders may then complete the current lap and return to the pit lane.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.2.4', 'G.4.2.4', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Development of the sessions', 'RACEOP', 'If a practice session is interrupted due to an incident or any other reason, a red flag will be shown at the start line and at all marshal posts. All riders must slow down and return safely to the pit lane. When the session is restarted, the remaining time will be the time displayed on the official timekeeping monitors and the pit lane countdown at the moment the red flag was shown.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.2.5', 'G.4.2.5', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Development of the sessions', 'RACEOP', 'If the number of authorized prototypes exceeds the maximum number allowed on track simultaneously, the Organization may divide the session into two groups.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.3.1', 'G.4.3.1', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Number and duration of Qualifying/Practices sessions for each Category', 'RACEOP', 'Two Free Practice session of 20 minutes for each Category. (TBC)', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.3.2', 'G.4.3.2', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Number and duration of Qualifying/Practices sessions for each Category', 'RACEOP', 'One Qualifying session of 20 minutes for each Category. (TBC)', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.3.3', 'G.4.3.3', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Number and duration of Qualifying/Practices sessions for each Category', 'RACEOP', 'One Warm-Up session of 15 minutes for each Category. (TBC)', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.4.1', 'G.4.4.1', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Lap Time', 'RACEOP', 'All laps will be timed.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.4.2', 'G.4.4.2', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Lap Time', 'RACEOP', 'Lap time is measured as the time elapsed between two consecutive crossings of the finish line timing plane.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.5.1', 'G.4.5.1', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Qualifying session results', 'RACEOP', 'The qualifying classification will be determined by the fastest lap time achieved by each rider during the Qualifying session.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.5.2', 'G.4.5.2', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Qualifying session results', 'RACEOP', 'If the Qualifying session is cancelled, the classification will be determined using the fastest lap time recorded during the Free Practice sessions.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.5.3', 'G.4.5.3', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Qualifying session results', 'RACEOP', 'In the event of a tie, the riders’ second-best lap times, and if necessary subsequent lap times, will be taken into account.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.5.4', 'G.4.5.4', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Qualifying session results', 'RACEOP', 'The Qualifying results will become final 30 minutes after publication of the provisional results. After this time, the results will not be subject to protest or appeal and will not be modified based on any infringements reported after this deadline. The Play-Off Race grid will be established according to these results.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.6.1', 'G.4.6.1', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Qualification for the Final Race', 'RACEOP', 'Direct qualification:
- Based on the Qualifying session results, the fastest half of the riders authorized to participate in the Qualifying session (rounded up to the nearest whole number) will qualify directly for the Final Race.
- Riders included in the authorized list who have not recorded a lap time during the Qualifying session will also be considered in this calculation.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.6.2', 'G.4.6.2', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Qualification for the Final Race', 'RACEOP', 'Promotion to the Final Race from the Play-Off Race:
- All riders authorized to participate in the Qualifying session who do not qualify directly for the Final Race will participate in the Play-Off Race.
- The 1st, 2nd and 3rd classified riders in the Play-Off Race will also qualify for the Final Race.
- If a team withdraws between the publication of the Qualifying results and the publication of the Final Race grid, the next classified rider from the Play-Off Race will be promoted to the Final Race.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.6.3', 'G.4.6.3', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Qualification for the Final Race', 'RACEOP', 'If the Play-Off Race is cancelled, qualification for the Final Race will require a lap time equal to or faster than 112% of the fastest lap recorded during the Qualifying session.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.6.4', 'G.4.6.4', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'Qualification for the Final Race', 'RACEOP', 'The Organization reserves the right to exclude any prototype considered to represent a safety risk for the race, based on factors such as lap times, track behaviour or top speed.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.7.1', 'G.4.7.1', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'MS2 tests carried out during sessions', 'RACEOP', 'Test 4 (Top Speed) will take place during the second Free Practice session.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.7.2', 'G.4.7.2', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'MS2 tests carried out during sessions', 'RACEOP', 'Test 6 (Pole Position) will take place during the Qualifying session.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.7.3', 'G.4.7.3', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'MS2 tests carried out during sessions', 'RACEOP', 'Test 5 (Regularity) will take place during the Warm-Up session.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.4.7.4', 'G.4.7.4', 'G', 4, 'Practice Sessions (Including Warm-Up)', 'MS2 tests carried out during sessions', 'RACEOP', 'Test 7 (Best Race Lap) and Test 8 (Race Result) will take place during the race sessions.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.5.1.1', 'G.5.1.1', 'G', 5, 'Grid Positions', 'Grid configuration', 'RACEOP', 'The starting grid will be arranged in a 3–3–3 configuration in staggered formation.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.5.1.2', 'G.5.1.2', 'G', 5, 'Grid Positions', 'Grid configuration', 'RACEOP', 'Each row will be offset.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.5.1.3', 'G.5.1.3', 'G', 5, 'Grid Positions', 'Grid configuration', 'RACEOP', 'The distance between rows will be 9 metres. Picture 48 - Starting grid positions', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.5.2.1', 'G.5.2.1', 'G', 5, 'Grid Positions', 'Grid Allocation', 'RACEOP', 'Play-Off Race Grid positions will be determined by the fastest lap time recorded during the Qualifying session. Teams not directly qualified for the Final Race will be placed on the grid in order of their Qualifying lap times, starting with the fastest.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.5.2.2', 'G.5.2.2', 'G', 5, 'Grid Positions', 'Grid Allocation', 'RACEOP', 'Final Race Grid positions will be determined based on the Qualifying session results and the results of the Play-Off Race. Riders directly qualified for the Final Race will occupy the first grid positions according to their Qualifying times. The riders promoted from the Play-Off Race will then be placed on the grid according to their finishing order in the Play-Off Race.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.5.2.3', 'G.5.2.3', 'G', 5, 'Grid Positions', 'Grid Allocation', 'RACEOP', 'If a team is unable to participate in the Qualifying session due to a technical problem or crash, Race Direction may authorize the team to participate in the Play- Off Race upon request, provided that the team has completed at least one full lap during the Free Practice sessions. In such case, the team will start from the last grid position. If multiple teams are in this situation, their order on the grid will be determined according to their best lap time achieved during their last Free Practice sessions.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.5.3.1', 'G.5.3.1', 'G', 5, 'Grid Positions', 'MS1 Handicaps', 'RACEOP', 'If a team has achieved less than 250 points in the MS1 Phase, a time handicap will be applied to its grid allocation time (Play-Off Race or Final Race grid allocation), but not to the promotion to the Final Race.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.5.3.2', 'G.5.3.2', 'G', 5, 'Grid Positions', 'MS1 Handicaps', 'RACEOP', 'If a team is not directly qualified for the Final Race, the handicap will only be applied for the Play-Off Race grid allocation. If the rider subsequently qualifies for the Final Race, the handicap will not be applied again.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.5.3.3', 'G.5.3.3', 'G', 5, 'Grid Positions', 'MS1 Handicaps', 'RACEOP', 'The handicap time applied according to the MS1 score is: Scoring intervals Handicap time 250 > MS1 Score ≥ 200 3” 200 > MS1 Score ≥ 150 7” 150 > MS1 Score ≥ 100 15” 100 > MS1 Score 30” Table 11 - Handicap time', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.1.1', 'G.6.1.1', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Number of races', 'RACEOP', 'During the Final Event each Category will run two (2) race sessions:
- Play-Off Race: Qualification session for the Final Race. The first three classified riders will qualify for the Final Race. Race distance: Electric Category: 6 laps eFuel Category: 6 laps
- Final Race: The final positions for the MS2 tests developed during the races will be determined in this race. Race distance: Electric Category: 7 laps eFuel Category: 9 laps', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.1.2', 'G.6.1.2', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Number of races', 'RACEOP', 'The Play-Off Race may be cancelled if the MS2 Sports Committee considers it necessary.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.1.3', 'G.6.1.3', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Number of races', 'RACEOP', 'Electric and eFuel categories will run independent races.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.2.1', 'G.6.2.1', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Start Procedures', 'RACEOP', 'Standard Start Procedure - eFuel Category 1. Approximately 40 minutes before the Start of the Race (except in the case of a restarted or rescheduled race), Race Direction will inform the teams via the official timing system if the race is declared “wet”. The race may also be declared “dry”, although this is not mandatory. If no information is displayed, the race will automatically be considered “dry”. 2. Only riders who have completed at least one sighting lap will be permitted to start the race from their published grid position. Under no circumstances may a rider push the motorcycle onto the grid from the pit lane. 3. Approximately 20 minutes before the Start of the Race (except in the case of a restarted or rescheduled race):
- Pit lane exit opens for sighting laps.
- Green lights are displayed at the pit lane exit.
- Count-down boards are shown at the pit exit. Riders may complete more than one sighting lap by passing through the pit lane, where adjustments may be made, tyres may be changed or refuelling may be carried out. 4. Approximately 15 minutes before the Start of the Race.
-Pit lane exit closes.
-Red lights are displayed at the pit lane exit. 5. Riders who do not proceed to the grid may start the warm-up lap from the pit lane under the instructions of the marshal positioned at the pit lane exit. Riders starting the warm-up lap from the pit lane must start the race from the back of the grid. 6. When riders arrive on the grid after the sighting lap(s), they must stop at the rear of the grid and switch off the engine. The motorcycle will then be pushed at walking pace by a Team Member to the assigned grid position. The rider may remain seated on the motorcycle or dismount while it is pushed. All persons present on the grid must wear a valid grid access pass. Officials will display panels indicating the grid rows to assist riders in locating their grid positions. 7. At this stage the Race Director will declare the race as “wet” or “dry” by displaying a board on the grid and in the pit lane. If no board is displayed the race will automatically be considered “dry”. 8. Riders on the grid may make adjustments to the motorcycle or change tyres according to track conditions. Tyre warmers may be used on the grid. One generator per prototype may be used exclusively to power tyre warmers. The generator must be a compact portable unit with a maximum output of 2 kW. Generators must be installed on a trolley with wheels and equipped with a closed tray capable of containing any potential fluid leakage. Any generator considered unsafe by the Technical Scrutineers will be removed immediately from the grid. The decision of the Technical Scrutineers is final. Generator trolleys must be positioned behind the prototypes. The size and type of grid equipment must allow rapid clearing of the grid and are subject to approval by the Organization. All adjustments must be completed before the display of the 3 Minutes board. After the display of the 3 Minutes board, any rider wishing to continue working on the motorcycle must push the motorcycle to the pit lane. The rider and motorcycle must be clear of the grid before the 1 Minute board is displayed. Work may then continue in the pit lane. Such riders will start the warm-up lap from the pit lane and will start the race from the back of the grid. 9. Refuelling or changing the fuel tank on the grid is strictly forbidden. 10. 5 Minutes before the Start of the Warm-Up Lap – the 5 Minutes board is displayed on the grid. 11. 3 Minutes before the Start of the Warm-Up Lap – the 3 Minutes board is displayed. Generators must be disconnected and all trolleys removed from the grid as quickly as possible. At this point only, the rider and three Team Members per team may remain on the grid. All other team personnel must leave the grid immediately. Riders must put their helmets on. No additional persons may access the grid after this point. 12. 1 Minute before the Start of the Warm-Up Lap – the 1 Minute board is displayed. Tyre warmers must be removed immediately. Engines must be started. Only the rider may remain on the grid. All Team Members must immediately leave the grid. 13. 30 Seconds before the Start of the Warm-Up Lap – the 30 Seconds board is displayed. Any rider whose engine is not running will be removed to the pit lane under the control of the grid marshals. Such riders may start the warm-up lap from the pit lane and will start the race from the back of the grid. 14. Approximately 5 minutes before the Start of the Race – the green flag is waved to start the warm-up lap. Riders will complete one lap at unrestricted speed followed by a Safety Car. The Safety Car may overtake slow riders. Any rider who stalls the engine on the grid or encounters a problem must signal by raising an arm. Under the supervision of an official the rider and motorcycle will be moved to the pit lane where mechanics may provide assistance. Such riders may start the warm-up lap from the pit lane and will start the race from the back of the grid, provided they exit before the pit lane closes and reach the grid before the Safety Car. If they do not exit before the pit lane closes they will start the race from the pit lane. When the riders who started from the grid pass the pit lane exit, the pit exit light will turn green to allow riders waiting in the pit lane to join the warm- up lap. Thirty seconds later the light will turn red closing the pit exit. If two or more riders must start from the back of the grid, they will line up in the order of their original grid positions. An official will stand at the front of the grid holding a stationary red flag. Any rider arriving at pit lane entry after the Safety Car must enter the pit lane and start the race from the pit lane exit. The reference lap time of the Safety Car will be 4’30”. Any rider encountering a problem during the warm-up lap may return to the pit lane for repairs. As each row of the grid is completed, the officials will lower the panels indicating that the row is correctly formed. When all panels have been lowered and the Safety Car has taken its position, an official at the rear of the grid will wave a green flag. The Starter will then instruct the official at the front of the grid, holding the red flag, to move to the side of the track. 15. Race Start. A red light will be displayed for between 2 and 5 seconds. When the red light goes out the race will start. A Safety Car will follow the motorcycles during the entire first lap and may overtake slow riders. Any rider who anticipates the start will be penalized by Race Direction. The standard penalty is two Long Lap Penalties. In case of minor movement Race Direction will be the sole judge of whether an advantage has been gained. 16. If a rider stalls the motorcycle after the start, officials will assist in pushing the motorcycle into the pit lane where the team may provide assistance. 17. After the riders pass the pit lane exit point, the green light will be switched on to allow riders still in the pit lane to start the race. A pit lane start will be made from a stationary position as directed by the officials. However, a rider who is delayed and arrives after the pit lane exit is open (and before it gets closed) will not be required to stop at pit exit before joining the race. If more than six riders must start the race from the pit lane, the start will be delayed and a Quick Start Procedure will be initiated. A rider starting from the pit lane may join the race until the race leader crosses the finish line to complete the first lap. 18. If a motorcycle that has been active in the race enters the pit box, it is considered retired and may not rejoin the race.', 'sporting', 'penalty', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.2.2', 'G.6.2.2', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Start Procedures', 'RACEOP', 'Standard Start Procedure - Electric Category 1. Approximately 40 minutes before the Start of the Race (except in the case of a restarted or rescheduled race), Race Direction will inform the teams via the official timing system if the race is declared "wet". The race may also be declared "dry", although this is not mandatory. If no information is displayed, the race will automatically be considered "dry". 2. Approximately 25 minutes before the Start of the Race. Teams must be ready in the “Slow Lane” of the Pit Lane in order to push their prototypes onto the grid through the pit wall access door. 3. Approximately 20 minutes before the Start of the Race (except in the case of a restarted or rescheduled race). The pit wall access to the grid will open for Teams and prototypes. 4. Approximately 15 minutes before the Start of the Race. Pit wall access to the grid will close. 5. Riders who do not go onto the grid may start the warm-up lap from the pit lane under the instructions of the marshal positioned at the pit lane exit. Riders starting the warm-up lap from the pit lane must start the race from the back of the grid. 6. When riders reach the grid through the pit wall, one mechanic must push the prototype at walking pace to the assigned grid position. The use of the electric motor to reach the grid is not permitted. All persons present on the grid must wear a valid grid access pass. Officials will display panels indicating the grid rows to assist riders in locating their grid positions. 7. At this stage the Race Director will declare the race as “wet” or “dry” by displaying a board on the grid and in the pit lane. If no board is displayed the race will automatically be considered “dry”. 8. Riders on the grid may make adjustments to the prototype or change tyres according to track conditions. Tyre warmers may be used on the grid. One generator per prototype may be used exclusively to power tyre warmers on the grid. The generator must not be powered by any kind of fuel and must consist of a sealed Pb battery (gel / AGM / sealed battery) together with a commercial sinusoidal wave inverter with a maximum output of 2 kW. All generators must be installed on a wheeled trolley and equipped with a closed tray capable of containing any possible fluid leakage. Any generator considered unsafe by the Technical Scrutineers will be removed immediately from the grid. The decision of the Technical Scrutineers will be final. Generator trolleys must be positioned behind the prototypes. To ensure rapid clearing of the grid, the size and type of grid equipment (including generator trolleys) are subject to approval by the Organization. All adjustments must be completed before the display of the 3 Minutes board. After the display of the 3 Minutes board, any rider wishing to continue adjustments must push the prototype to the pit lane. The rider and prototype must be clear of the grid before the 1 Minute board is displayed. Work may then continue in the pit lane. Such riders will start the warm-up lap from the pit lane and will start the race from the back of the grid. 9. Charging the prototype battery on the grid is strictly forbidden at all times. 10. 5 Minutes before the Start of the Warm-Up Lap – the 5 Minutes board will be displayed on the grid. 11. 3 Minutes before the Start of the Warm-Up Lap – the 3 Minutes board will be displayed. Generators must be disconnected and all trolleys must be removed from the grid as quickly as possible. At this point only the rider and three Team Members per team may remain on the grid. All other team personnel must leave the grid immediately. Riders must put their helmets on. No additional persons may access the grid after this moment. 12. 1 Minute before the Start of the Warm-Up Lap – the 1 Minute board will be displayed. Tyre warmers must be removed immediately. Prototypes must be powered on and ready to race. Only the rider may remain on the grid. All Team Members must immediately vacate the grid. 13. 30 Seconds before the Start of the Warm-Up Lap – the 30 Seconds board will be displayed. Any rider whose prototype is not powered on will be removed to the pit lane under the control of the grid marshals. Such riders may start the warm- up lap from the pit lane and will start the race from the back of the grid. 14. Approximately 5 minutes before the Start of the Race – the green flag will be waved to start the warm-up lap. Any rider who stalls the powertrain on the grid or encounters another problem must signal by raising an arm. Attempting to restart the prototype on the grid is not permitted. Under the supervision of an official, the rider and prototype will be moved to the pit lane where mechanics may provide assistance. Such riders may start the warm-up lap from the pit lane and will start the race from the back of the grid, provided they exit before the pit lane is closed and reach the grid before the Safety Car. If they do not exit before the pit lane closes, they will start the race from the pit lane. Riders will complete one lap at unrestricted speed followed by a Safety Car. The Safety Car may overtake slow riders. When the riders who started from the grid pass the pit lane exit, the pit lane exit light will turn green to allow riders waiting in the pit lane to join the warm-up lap. Thirty seconds later the light will turn red closing the pit exit. If two or more riders must start from the back of the grid, they will line up in the order of their original grid positions. An official will stand at the front of the grid holding a stationary red flag. Any rider arriving at the pit lane entry point after the Safety Car must enter the pit lane and start the race from the pit lane exit. The reference lap time of the Safety Car will be 4’30”. Any rider encountering a problem during the warm-up lap may return to the pit lane to make repairs. As each row of the grid is completed, officials will lower the panels indicating that the row is correctly formed. When all panels have been lowered and the Safety Car has taken its position, an official at the rear of the grid will wave a green flag. The Starter will then instruct the official at the front of the grid, holding the red flag, to move to the side of the track. 15. Race Start. A red light will be displayed for between 2 and 5 seconds. When the red light goes out the race will start. A Safety Car will follow the motorcycles for the entire first lap and may overtake slow riders. Any rider who anticipates the start will be penalized by Race Direction. The standard penalty is two Long Lap Penalties. In case of minor movement, Race Direction will be the sole judge of whether an advantage has been gained. 16. If a rider stalls the prototype after the start, officials will assist in pushing the motorcycle into the pit lane where the Team may provide assistance. 17. After the riders pass the pit lane exit point, the green light at the pit lane exit will be switched on to allow riders still in the pit lane to start the race. A pit lane race start will be made from a stationary position as directed by the officials. However, a rider who is delayed and arrives after the pit lane exit is open (and before it gets closed) will not be required to stop at pit exit before joining the race. If more than six riders must start the race from the pit lane, the start will be delayed and a Quick Start Procedure will take place. Any rider starting the race from the pit lane may join the race until the race leader crosses the finish line to complete the first lap. 18. If a prototype that has been active in the race enters the pit box, the prototype will be considered retired and may not re-enter the race.', 'sporting', 'penalty', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.2.3', 'G.6.2.3', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Start Procedures', 'RACEOP', 'Start Delayed If any problem occurs during the start procedure that may represent a safety risk, the Starter will invoke the Start Delayed procedure as follows:
- A red flag will be waved from the Starter’s rostrum and the red start light will remain on.
- The Starter will display the “Start Delayed” board and marshals will wave yellow flags at each row of the starting grid.
- Riders must remain in their grid positions with helmets on. Engines may be switched off.
- The prototype that caused the Start Delayed will be removed to the pit lane, regardless of whether the problem can be solved before the new start. If the problem is resolved, the rider may start the warm-up lap from the pit lane and will start the race from the back of the grid.
- After the Start Delayed board is displayed, only two Team Members per prototype are allowed to remain on the grid. Only tyre warmers and stands are permitted. Generators and trolleys are not allowed on the grid.
- As soon as possible the start procedure will be resumed from the 3 Minutes board.
- After the 30 Seconds board is displayed, riders will complete one additional warm-up lap and the race distance will automatically be reduced by one lap. If Race Direction considers it necessary, the race distance may be reduced by more than one lap.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.2.4', 'G.6.2.4', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Start Procedures', 'RACEOP', 'Quick Start Procedure When a race is stopped, riders must return to the pit lane unless otherwise instructed by officials. If the race is to be restarted, minor repairs may be carried out. The following procedure will apply:
- Upon arrival in the pit lane, Teams may make adjustments to their machine. Refuelling is permitted in pit boxes for the eFuel Category and Recharging is permitted in the pit lane for the Electric Category.
- When all riders have entered the pit lane, the Race Director will announce the time remaining until the re-opening of the pit lane.
a) The time between the red flag and the opening of the pit lane exit will be a minimum of 10 minutes.
b) The re-opening time will be published on the timing screens and may also be communicated to Teams through any other official communication channel. Count-down boards may be displayed at the pit lane exit.
- When this time period has elapsed:
a) (For eFuel Category) The pit lane will be opened for SIXTY SECONDS only. Riders will complete one lap at unrestricted speed to the starting grid, followed by a Safety Car. Any rider delaying the progress of the sighting lap may be overtaken by the Safety Car. Any rider arriving behind the Safety Car must enter the pit lane. Such riders must start the warm-up lap from the pit lane and will start the race from the back of the grid.
b) (For Electric Category) The pit wall access will be opened for TWO MINUTES only. Prototypes will be placed in their grid positions.
- Any riders remaining in the pit lane after the pit lane exit or pit wall access has been closed must start the warm-up lap from the pit lane exit and will start the race from the back of the grid.
- After the closure of the pit lane exit or pit wall access, tyre warmers must be removed from all machines remaining in the pit lane.
- Only one Team Member per prototype is allowed on the grid, without tools, solely to indicate the rider’s grid position.
- Once the rider reaches their grid position, the mechanic must immediately leave the grid.
- For the eFuel Category, engines must remain running on the grid. For the Electric Category, prototypes must be powered on as soon as they reach their grid positions.
- As soon as the Safety Car arrives at the rear of the grid, a 30 Seconds board will be displayed. These 30 seconds may be reduced at the discretion of Race Direction if the grid is cleared and conditions are considered safe.
- After the 30 seconds have elapsed, a green flag will be shown to start the warm-up lap.
- The warm-up lap will be completed at unrestricted speed, followed by a Safety Car. At the end of the warm-up lap, the normal start procedure will apply and the race will start in the standard manner.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[{"op": "min", "value": 10.0, "unit": "minutes"}]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.2.5', 'G.6.2.5', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Start Procedures', 'RACEOP', 'If a race in the Electric Category is declared “wet” while all previous sessions have been run in “dry” conditions, the start procedure of the eFuel Category will apply and the race distance will be reduced by one lap.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.2.6', 'G.6.2.6', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Start Procedures', 'RACEOP', 'If a race in the eFuel Category is declared “wet” while all previous sessions have been run in “dry” conditions, the standard start procedure for that category will apply.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.3.1', 'G.6.3.1', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Finish of a Race and Race Results', 'RACEOP', 'When the leading rider has completed the designated race distance, he/she will be shown the Chequered Flag by an official positioned at the finish line behind the first protection line. The Chequered Flag will continue to be displayed to the subsequent riders. Once the Chequered Flag has been shown to the leading rider, no other rider will be permitted to enter the track from the pit lane. Immediately after the Chequered Flag is shown to the leading rider, the red light will be switched on at the pit lane exit and a marshal displaying a red flag will take position at the pit lane exit. If a rider closely precedes the leader during the final lap before the finish line, the official will show the Chequered Flag together with the Blue Flag simultaneously to both the leader and the rider(s) concerned. This indicates that the race has finished for the leader, while the rider(s) concerned must complete their lap and then take the Chequered Flag.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.3.2', 'G.6.3.2', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Finish of a Race and Race Results', 'RACEOP', 'To be classified as a finisher in the race and be included in the official results, a rider must:
a) Complete at least 75% of the race distance, expressed in laps and rounded up to the nearest whole number of laps.
b) Cross the finish line on the race track (not in the pit lane) within five minutes of the race winner. If the rider is not in contact with the prototype when crossing the finish line, the finishing time will be determined by the last part of either the rider or the prototype to cross the finish line.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.3.3', 'G.6.3.3', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Finish of a Race and Race Results', 'RACEOP', 'The race results will be determined according to the order in which riders cross the finish line and the number of laps completed.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.3.4', 'G.6.3.4', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Finish of a Race and Race Results', 'RACEOP', 'In the event of a photo-finish between two or more riders, the result will be decided in favour of the rider whose front wheel leading edge crosses the plane of the finish line first. If the rider is not in contact with the prototype when crossing the finish line, the finishing time will be determined by the last part of either the rider or the prototype to cross the finish line.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.3.5', 'G.6.3.5', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Finish of a Race and Race Results', 'RACEOP', 'At the end of the race, all prototypes that have taken the start must proceed to Parc Fermé under the instructions of the officials. This requirement applies whether the prototype has finished the race, retired, entered the pit box, or been removed from the track due to an incident. No work or intervention may be carried out on the prototype after the race unless authorized by the Technical Scrutineers or Race Direction. Failure to comply with this requirement may result in disqualification from the race.', 'sporting', 'blocking', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.3.6', 'G.6.3.6', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Finish of a Race and Race Results', 'RACEOP', 'For the Electric Category only, the victory lap and return to Parc Fermé will be carried out using the “National Track” layout (2,379.12 m).', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.4.1', 'G.6.4.1', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Interruption of a Race', 'RACEOP', 'If the Race Director decides to interrupt a race at any point from the start of the warm-up lap onwards, red flags will be displayed at the finish line and at all marshals’ posts, and red lights around the circuit will be switched on.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.4.2', 'G.6.4.2', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Interruption of a Race', 'RACEOP', 'The race results will be established taking into consideration the last point at which the leader had completed a full lap without the red flag being displayed. The classification will be established as follows:
a) For riders who crossed the finish line on the same lap as the leader before the red flag was displayed, a partial classification will be established at the end of that lap.
b) For riders who had not crossed the finish line on the same lap as the leader before the red flag was displayed, a partial classification will be established at the end of the previous lap.
c) The complete classification will be established by combining both partial classifications according to the lap/time procedure.
d) Riders who have entered the pit lane which is then closed due to the red flag may be classified according to the number of laps completed and the time of crossing the virtual finish line in the pit lane as follows:
- If the rider has crossed the virtual finish line in the pit lane, the rider’s position will be determined based on that crossing.
- If the rider has not crossed the virtual finish line in the pit lane, the rider’s last crossing of the track finish line will be used.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.4.3', 'G.6.4.3', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Interruption of a Race', 'RACEOP', 'At the moment the red flag is displayed, riders who are not actively competing in the race will not be classified.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.4.4', 'G.6.4.4', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Interruption of a Race', 'RACEOP', 'Within five minutes after the red flag has been displayed, riders who have not entered the pit lane, crossing the designated pit lane entry timing point together with their prototype, will not be classified. An exemption may be granted in exceptional circumstances (e.g. post-race celebration in an interrupted race deemed to have been completed).', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.4.5', 'G.6.4.5', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Interruption of a Race', 'RACEOP', 'If more than two thirds of the original race distance have been completed by the leader of the race, rounded down to the nearest whole number of laps, the race will be deemed completed and full points will be awarded.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.4.6', 'G.6.4.6', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Interruption of a Race', 'RACEOP', 'If less than two thirds of the original race distance have been completed by the leader of the race, rounded down to the nearest whole number of laps, the race will be restarted according to Article G.6.5. If it is not possible to restart the race, the results will be awarded as follows:
- Less than 50%* of the original race distance completed = Null Race, no points awarded.
- More than 50%* of the original race distance completed = Full points awarded. *50% rounded down to the nearest whole number of laps.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.4.7', 'G.6.4.7', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Interruption of a Race', 'RACEOP', 'For the purposes of these Rules & Regulations, “active” and “actively competing” are defined as a rider riding on track, attempting to repair or restart the engine / motor, or attempting to rejoin the track or return to the pit lane with the prototype in a condition fit to rejoin the race. Race Direction will be the sole judge of whether a rider is actively competing, including the condition of the prototype. No appeal is possible against the decision of Race Direction.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.5.1', 'G.6.5.1', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Re-Starting a Race that has been interrupted', 'RACEOP', 'Re-started races will, in principle, follow the procedures defined in this Article. However, as local track, climatic conditions, and other circumstances may vary, Race Direction may reschedule a re-started race within the race program if necessary. Race Direction will make the final decision on whether, when, and how many times an interrupted race will be re-started, according to the circumstances. Note that in all cases of restarted races, the calculation of the race distance required to declare a result (2/3 distance) will be based on the number of laps of the current race, and not on the original race distance.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.5.2', 'G.6.5.2', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Re-Starting a Race that has been interrupted', 'RACEOP', 'If a race has to be re-started, the time at which the new start procedure will begin will be displayed on the timekeeping screens. Additionally, this information may also be communicated to Teams through any of the official communication channels of the Organization.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.5.3', 'G.6.5.3', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Re-Starting a Race that has been interrupted', 'RACEOP', 'For any race that is re-started, the start procedure will follow the Quick Start Procedure.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.6.5.4', 'G.6.5.4', 'G', 6, 'Races', 'Re-Starting a Race that has been interrupted', 'RACEOP', 'The conditions for the re-started race will be as follows:
a) If less than three laps have been completed:
- All riders may start, including riders who may not have completed the sighting lap or warm-up lap for the original start.
- Prototypes may be repaired.
- Refuelling or recharging is permitted.
- The race distance will be the number of laps required to complete the original race distance.
- Grid positions will be the same as for the original race.
b) If three laps or more than three laps have been completed but less than two thirds of the race distance:
- Only riders classified in the interrupted race may re-start. To be eligible to re-start, the rider must enter the pit lane, riding or pushing the prototype, within five minutes after the red flag was displayed in the interrupted race (using the homologated track).
- Prototypes may be repaired.
- Refuelling or recharging is permitted.
- The race distance will be the number of laps required to complete the original race distance.
- Grid positions will be determined according to the classification at the moment of the interruption (Article G.6.5.2).', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.7.1.1', 'G.7.1.1', 'G', 7, 'Parc Fermé', 'Parc Fermé (closed park area)', 'RACEOP', 'Parc Fermé is a controlled area used during the Final Event to ensure sporting fairness and to allow the Technical Organization to verify that the motorcycles comply with the Technical Regulations following a practice session, qualifying session or race. When a motorcycle is placed in Parc Fermé, no intervention, modification, adjustment or work of any kind may be carried out on the motorcycle unless expressly authorized by the Technical Director or Technical Staff. Any motorcycle required to enter Parc Fermé must proceed there immediately after the relevant session and remain under the supervision of the Technical Organization until released.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.7.2.1', 'G.7.2.1', 'G', 7, 'Parc Fermé', 'Practice Sessions', 'RACEOP', 'At the end of any practice session or on-track test, the first three classified prototypes of the session, or in any test performed during the session, may be required to proceed at the Technical Control Area in order to perform any checks requested by the Chief Scrutineer. Additionally, other prototypes may be selected at random and directed to the Technical Control Area by the Technical Stewards for inspection.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.7.3.1', 'G.7.3.1', 'G', 7, 'Parc Fermé', 'Race Sessions', 'RACEOP', 'At the end of a race, or after the final part of a race that has been interrupted, all prototypes must proceed directly to the Parc Fermé area designated by the Competition Organization. In this area the prototypes shall remain at the disposal of the Technical Stewards until their release is authorized, in order to allow:
- Technical inspections
- Regulatory compliance checks
- Verification in case of protests or technical investigations It is the responsibility of the Teams and riders to ensure that their prototype is brought to Parc Fermé in accordance with the instructions of the officials. This requirement applies to all prototypes that have taken the start of the race, whether they have finished the race, retired, entered the pit box, or been removed from the track due to an incident. Once the prototype has crossed the finish line, no work, intervention or adjustment of any kind may be carried out on the motorcycle unless expressly authorized by the Technical Stewards or Race Direction. Failure to comply with Parc Fermé procedures may result in disqualification from the race.', 'sporting', 'blocking', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.7.4.1', 'G.7.4.1', 'G', 7, 'Parc Fermé', 'Parc Fermé responsibility and selection for inspection', 'RACEOP', 'It is the sole responsibility of the Team and the rider to ensure that the prototype proceeds immediately to Parc Fermé when required. The selection of prototypes for technical inspection may take place without prior notice and forms part of the standard technical control procedures. The Technical Director, Technical Stewards or Race Direction may require any prototype to proceed to Parc Fermé or to undergo technical inspection at any time during the Competition.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.8.1.1', 'G.8.1.1', 'G', 8, 'Abandonement During The Event', 'Notification of Withdrawal', 'RACEOP', 'Any Team entered in the Final Event must inform the Organization if, at any time, they decide not to participate in the event or decide to withdraw during the Event.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.8.2.1', 'G.8.2.1', 'G', 8, 'Abandonement During The Event', 'Abandonment Process', 'RACEOP', 'If a Team is unable to continue in the competition due to irreparable technical problems, rider injury, or any other reason, the Team Leader or Faculty Advisor must report to the Paddock General Office in order to formally declare the Team’s abandonment. Once the abandonment has been declared, the engine / motor must be immediately returned to the Technical Inspection Area or to any other location designated by the Organization for its return and subsequent inspection and rebuilding. The prototype shall also remain available for possible technical checks if requested by the Technical Staff.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.8.2.2', 'G.8.2.2', 'G', 8, 'Abandonement During The Event', 'Abandonment Process', 'RACEOP', 'The abandonment declaration is irreversible. Once a Team has formally declared its abandonment, it will not be permitted to participate in any remaining sessions or races, even if the original issue has been resolved.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.1.1', 'G.9.1.1', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Rider behaviour', 'RACEOP', 'Riders must strictly follow the instructions given by the marshals at all times.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.1.2', 'G.9.1.2', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Rider behaviour', 'RACEOP', 'Riders must circulate at a calm and moderate speed when transiting between tests. This requirement applies to all movements within the test area during Rounds 1 and 2 of Tests 1, 2 and 3.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.2.1', 'G.9.2.1', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Test Rounds Layout', 'RACEOP', 'The entry point for all rounds of Tests 1, 2 and 3 will be located at the pit entry.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.2.2', 'G.9.2.2', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Test Rounds Layout', 'RACEOP', 'The exit point for all rounds of Tests 1, 2 and 3 will be located at the pit exit.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.2.3', 'G.9.2.3', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Test Rounds Layout', 'RACEOP', 'During these rounds, circulation inside the Pit Lane will be in the opposite direction to the normal racing direction of the circuit.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.2.4', 'G.9.2.4', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Test Rounds Layout', 'RACEOP', 'The approximate location of the tests will be as follows: Figure 49 - Rounds 1 and 2 layouts', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.3.1', 'G.9.3.1', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Waiting Area Regulations', 'RACEOP', 'A designated waiting area will be established at the entrance of each test round.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.3.2', 'G.9.3.2', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Waiting Area Regulations', 'RACEOP', 'Each prototype will be assigned access to three electrical outlets within the waiting area.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.3.3', 'G.9.3.3', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Waiting Area Regulations', 'RACEOP', 'Only two Team Members and one rider per team are allowed inside the waiting area.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.3.4', 'G.9.3.4', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Waiting Area Regulations', 'RACEOP', 'The only permitted equipment in the waiting area are two tyre warmers (front and rear) and one cooling or heating fan for the thermal management of the prototype.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.3.5', 'G.9.3.5', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Waiting Area Regulations', 'RACEOP', 'Marshals will indicate the starting order of the rounds based on the arrival order of the teams in the waiting area.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.3.6', 'G.9.3.6', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Waiting Area Regulations', 'RACEOP', 'If a team refuses to proceed with the test when instructed by the marshals, the round will be recorded as NP (Not Performed) for that team.', 'sporting', 'penalty', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.3.7', 'G.9.3.7', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Waiting Area Regulations', 'RACEOP', 'Any incident or interference with the correct operation of the test may be penalised by Race Direction depending on the severity of the infringement.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.4.1', 'G.9.4.1', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Time Control Procedure', 'RACEOP', 'All rounds of Tests 1, 2 and 3 will be subject to a time control procedure.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.4.2', 'G.9.4.2', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Time Control Procedure', 'RACEOP', 'The time control will be located in the designated tent within the waiting area.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.4.3', 'G.9.4.3', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Time Control Procedure', 'RACEOP', 'The rider and the prototype in operational condition must be present in the waiting area at the exact scheduled time published by the Organization.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.4.4', 'G.9.4.4', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Time Control Procedure', 'RACEOP', 'Teams arriving earlier than their scheduled time must wait in the area indicated by the marshals.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('G.9.4.5', 'G.9.4.5', 'G', 9, 'Test 1, 2 & 3 Behavior', 'Time Control Procedure', 'RACEOP', 'If a rider arrives after the scheduled control time, participation in that round will not be permitted and the round will be recorded as NP. SECTI ON H: FI NAL EVE NT SECTION H FINAL EVENT', 'sporting', 'penalty', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.1.1.1', 'H.1.1.1', 'H', 1, 'Schedule', 'Official Schedules during the Final Event', 'RACEOP', 'The Organization will establish an official schedule assigning each team the corresponding time slots to carry out the tests related to Scrutineering, the MS1 Phase and the MS2 Phase. These schedules will be published and communicated to the teams prior to the Final Event.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.1.1.2', 'H.1.1.2', 'H', 1, 'Schedule', 'Official Schedules during the Final Event', 'RACEOP', 'Teams must comply with the schedules established by the Organization during the Final Event. Failure to respect the assigned schedule may result in a penalty in the corresponding test or, if operational conditions require it, exclusion from that test.', 'sporting', 'penalty', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.1.1.3', 'H.1.1.3', 'H', 1, 'Schedule', 'Official Schedules during the Final Event', 'RACEOP', 'In the MotoStudent Electric Category, a minimum interval of 40 minutes between tests will be guaranteed to allow teams to recharge the battery.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.1.1.4', 'H.1.1.4', 'H', 1, 'Schedule', 'Official Schedules during the Final Event', 'RACEOP', 'The Organization reserves the right to modify the schedule of the tests if required for operational or safety reasons. The Organization will make every effort to ensure the efficient development of the Final Event and to provide teams with sufficient time to prepare between tests.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.1', 'H.2.1.1', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Participating teams undertake to respect and take care of the facilities where the Final Event takes place. Any misuse or damage to the facilities may result in sanctions imposed by the Organization, including expulsion from the Competition.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.2', 'H.2.1.2', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Annex 3 provides an indicative distribution of the different areas of the Final Event described below. The final layout will be confirmed in the Event Guide for Teams document.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.3', 'H.2.1.3', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Start–Finish Straight The finish straight of the FIM Grand Prix International circuit at MotorLand Aragón. In addition to being the starting and finishing point of the races, this straight will host several dynamic tests of the MS2 Phase of the Competition, as well as other parallel activities.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.4', 'H.2.1.4', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Pit Lane The route connecting the circuit layout with the Team Boxes. Access to this area is restricted to registered students, tutors and riders participating in the Competition. Public access to the Pit Lane is strictly prohibited.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.5', 'H.2.1.5', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Pit Building The main building of the circuit, composed of three floors:
- Ground Floor: Team Boxes, bathrooms and showers.
- First Floor: presentation rooms, media centre, restaurant, services, bathrooms, terraces and briefing room.
- Second Floor: public terraces. The floors are connected by stairways through Towers A, B, C, D, E and F. Tower E includes an elevator accessible for people with reduced mobility.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.6', 'H.2.1.6', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Public Terraces Located along the Pit Building, these terraces are open to the public to observe the activities taking place on track.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.7', 'H.2.1.7', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Media Centre Dedicated workspace for accredited media professionals and the MotoStudent communication team. The Media Centre provides working facilities for journalists, photographers and broadcasters covering the Final Event. Access to the Media Centre is restricted to media personnel accredited by the Organization. The Organization reserves the right to regulate access and use of the facilities.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.8', 'H.2.1.8', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Team Boxes Working garages assigned to the teams during the Final Event.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.9', 'H.2.1.9', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Technical Control Area Scrutineering area where the Organization performs the technical inspections of the participating prototypes (Static Scrutineering).', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.10', 'H.2.1.10', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'MotoStudent General Office Main office of the Competition Organization responsible for assisting registered teams during the Final Event.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.11', 'H.2.1.11', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Paddock General Office (PGO) Paddock office where teams may be summoned by different organizational committees (MS1, MS2, Technical, Disciplinary, etc.) to address matters related to protests, irregularities, disciplinary procedures or organizational issues.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.12', 'H.2.1.12', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'MotoStudent Shop Official shop of the Organization. During the Final Event, payments may be made in cash (€) or by credit card. Picture 50 - Accepted credit cards', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.13', 'H.2.1.13', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Tires Technical Service Service point for the supply and mounting of tyres.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.14', 'H.2.1.14', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Fuel Area Facility designated for the supply of the Official Fuel.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.15', 'H.2.1.15', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Dynamic Area Paddock area reserved for dynamic activities, including the Dynamic Safety Check and the regulated practice areas.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.16', 'H.2.1.16', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Parc Fermé Closed control area where prototypes may be retained for technical inspection after sessions or races.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.17', 'H.2.1.17', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'MotoStudent Arena Paddock area where official activities such as the MS1 Awards Ceremony, presentations and other event activities will take place.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.18', 'H.2.1.18', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Fan Zone Area dedicated to commercial activities, exhibitions and entertainment for visitors.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.19', 'H.2.1.19', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Medical Centre Medical facility providing healthcare assistance during the Final Event.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.1.20', 'H.2.1.20', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Definition of Areas', 'RACEOP', 'Working Vehicles Parking Area reserved for operational vehicles used by teams and Organization, with a maximum vehicle length of 8 meters.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.2.1', 'H.2.2.1', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Team Installations', 'RACEOP', 'The Organization will provide and assign, free of charge, a working area (located inside a Team Box) to each team. All repairs, adjustments and preparation of the prototype must be carried out in this area.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.2.2', 'H.2.2.2', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Team Installations', 'RACEOP', 'The Team Boxes are equipped with 230V power sockets with European standard plugs, as well as 230V industrial sockets and three-phase 400V sockets. The boxes also include a TV connection with access to live timing, compressed air supply, water connections and access to bathroom facilities.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.2.2.3', 'H.2.2.3', 'H', 2, 'Areas And Facilities During The Final Event', 'Team Installations', 'RACEOP', 'Personal and transport vehicles must be parked only in the areas designated for this purpose. Access to the track and test areas is restricted to vehicles authorized by the Organization.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.3.1.1', 'H.3.1.1', 'H', 3, 'Participant Accreditation', 'Accreditation', 'RACEOP', 'Upon arrival at the Final Event, the Organization will provide an accreditation pass and wristband to each registered Team Member, rider and tutor. This identification will allow the Organization to monitor participation in the different tests and any interventions carried out on the prototype.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.3.1.2', 'H.3.1.2', 'H', 3, 'Participant Accreditation', 'Accreditation', 'RACEOP', 'Accreditation passes and wristbands will be issued to registered Team Members upon entry to the Final Event and must be worn visibly at all times during the event. The accreditation passes and bracelets will be placed to the registered Team Members at the time of entering the Final Event, and they must wear them until it finishes.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.3.1.3', 'H.3.1.3', 'H', 3, 'Participant Accreditation', 'Accreditation', 'RACEOP', 'Accreditation passes and wristbands will only be issued to officially registered members of the team. Any person accompanying the team who is not officially registered will be considered part of the general public and will therefore not have the same access rights or operational privileges as registered participants.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.4.1.1', 'H.4.1.1', 'H', 4, 'Behaviour Rules', 'Behaviour of Participants during the Final Event', 'RACEOP', 'To ensure a safe and respectful environment during the Final Event, the following actions are strictly prohibited:
- Cooking inside the Boxes or in any areas not specifically authorized by the Organization.
- Sleeping inside the Boxes.
- Installing tents in areas not specifically authorized by the Organization.
- Bringing pets into the Paddock.
- Smoking, lighting fires, or storing gas containers inside the Boxes.
- Parking unauthorized vehicles inside the Paddock.
- Exchanging personal or vehicle accreditation passes.
- Painting, drilling, disassembling or otherwise damaging circuit facilities.
- Carrying out any commercial activity that may compromise public health or safety.
- Driving in a reckless manner inside the Paddock. Reckless driving includes driving without all tyres in contact with the ground, driving at speeds inappropriate for pedestrian safety, or carrying more passengers than permitted by local regulations and/or circuit rules. The use of helmets (for motorcycles) or safety belts (for cars) is mandatory.
- Walking around the Paddock stripped to the waist or wearing only sandals.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.4.1.2', 'H.4.1.2', 'H', 4, 'Behaviour Rules', 'Behaviour of Participants during the Final Event', 'RACEOP', 'Alcohol and Drugs The consumption, possession or influence of alcohol, drugs or any substance that may impair the physical or mental condition of participants is strictly prohibited during the Final Event. This prohibition applies to all participants including Team Members, riders, tutors and any accredited personnel. The Organization reserves the right to carry out checks whenever it considers necessary. Any person found under the influence of alcohol or drugs may be immediately removed from the Event and may lead to penalties or disqualification of the Team.', 'sporting', 'blocking', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.4.2.1', 'H.4.2.1', 'H', 4, 'Behaviour Rules', 'Authorized Vehicles in the Paddock', 'RACEOP', 'The prototype may only move under its own power during official tests. For any other movement within the Paddock, it must be pushed or moved with the engine or motor switched off.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.4.2.2', 'H.4.2.2', 'H', 4, 'Behaviour Rules', 'Authorized Vehicles in the Paddock', 'RACEOP', 'Vehicle circulation inside the Paddock is restricted to Organization vehicles and the following light vehicles:
- Non-motorized vehicles (scooters, bicycles, etc.).
- Personal mobility vehicles (electric scooters, assisted bicycles, etc.).
- Small scooters.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.4.2.3', 'H.4.2.3', 'H', 4, 'Behaviour Rules', 'Authorized Vehicles in the Paddock', 'RACEOP', 'The circulation of any vehicle on the Pit Lane (except for prototypes) is strictly prohibited, except for the use of non-motorized vehicles during the time allowed for track inspection.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.4.2.4', 'H.4.2.4', 'H', 4, 'Behaviour Rules', 'Authorized Vehicles in the Paddock', 'RACEOP', 'The circulation of the vehicles described in Article H.4.2.2 must comply with the following rules:
- No more than two persons may travel on the vehicle.
- Children under 14 years of age are not allowed to drive any vehicle.
- Reckless driving inside the Paddock is strictly prohibited.
- Vehicle circulation is prohibited during quiet hours (23:00 – 07:00).
- The use of a helmet is mandatory.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.4.3.1', 'H.4.3.1', 'H', 4, 'Behaviour Rules', 'Prototype Manipulation', 'RACEOP', 'For safety reasons, any manipulation of the prototype must comply with the following rules. Failure to comply may result in penalties or even expulsion from the Competition.', 'sporting', 'penalty', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.4.3.2', 'H.4.3.2', 'H', 4, 'Behaviour Rules', 'Prototype Manipulation', 'RACEOP', 'All repairs and manipulations of the prototype during the Final Event must be carried out exclusively inside the Team Box assigned to each team.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.4.3.3', 'H.4.3.3', 'H', 4, 'Behaviour Rules', 'Prototype Manipulation', 'RACEOP', 'The prototype must remain within the circuit facilities during the entire Final Event. The prototype, or any of its components (including batteries, fuel systems or critical parts), may not be removed from the circuit facilities under any circumstance without the explicit authorization of the Organization. Exceptionally, the Organization may authorize the temporary transfer of the prototype to the designated karting practice area under controlled conditions and only within the MotorLand facilities. Any unauthorized removal of the prototype or its components from the circuit may result in penalties or exclusion from the Competition.', 'sporting', 'penalty', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.5.1.1', 'H.5.1.1', 'H', 5, 'Communication', 'Contact with the Organization during the Final Event', 'RACEOP', 'Communication between teams and the Organization during the Final Event must be carried out primarily through the MotoStudent General Office.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.5.1.2', 'H.5.1.2', 'H', 5, 'Communication', 'Contact with the Organization during the Final Event', 'RACEOP', 'During the Final Event, the Team Tutor, Team Leader or rider may be summoned by the Organization to report incidents or address operational matters. Teams must attend these calls at the indicated location within a maximum period of 15 minutes from the moment the notification is issued.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.5.2.1', 'H.5.2.1', 'H', 5, 'Communication', 'Briefings', 'RACEOP', 'During the Final Event, the Organization will hold several briefings to explain the development of the Competition to teams, tutors and riders.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.5.2.2', 'H.5.2.2', 'H', 5, 'Communication', 'Briefings', 'RACEOP', 'Team Leaders, tutors or riders must attend the briefings when summoned by the Organization. Failure to attend without justified cause may result in penalties.', 'sporting', 'penalty', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.5.3.1', 'H.5.3.1', 'H', 5, 'Communication', 'Communication of Schedules and Results', 'RACEOP', 'The Organization will communicate the schedules of tests and sessions through different official communication channels.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.5.3.2', 'H.5.3.2', 'H', 5, 'Communication', 'Communication of Schedules and Results', 'RACEOP', 'The Organization will publish the results obtained in each test on the official notice board located in the Paddock.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.5.3.3', 'H.5.3.3', 'H', 5, 'Communication', 'Communication of Schedules and Results', 'RACEOP', 'The timing results of the “Free Practice”, “Qualifying” and “Race” sessions will be broadcast live through the circuit’s internal TV signal. In addition to screens located in common areas, all Team Boxes and the Pit Wall will have TV connections to access the live timing broadcast.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.5.3.4', 'H.5.3.4', 'H', 5, 'Communication', 'Communication of Schedules and Results', 'RACEOP', 'The timing results of the “Free Practice”, “Qualifying” and “Race” sessions will also be broadcast live via the internet. The Organization will communicate to the teams the web platform where live timing can be followed.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.5.3.5', 'H.5.3.5', 'H', 5, 'Communication', 'Communication of Schedules and Results', 'RACEOP', 'The final results obtained in each test may be published through the official communication channels of the Competition once the Competition has concluded.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.6.1.1', 'H.6.1.1', 'H', 6, 'Electrical Safety', 'Individual Safety Protections', 'RACEOP', 'In addition to the mandatory elements specified in Article D.5.3, the use of the following protective equipment is strongly recommended:
- Helmet or protective visor against fire or electric arc hazards.
- Insulated protective boots.
- Insulating mat CEI 61111 – Class 0.
- Emergency hook (CEI 61235 / CEI 60230 / CEI 50508 / NF C18-510).', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.6.1.2', 'H.6.1.2', 'H', 6, 'Electrical Safety', 'Individual Safety Protections', 'RACEOP', 'It is strongly recommended that students who will work with the electric prototype have completed a High Voltage safety training course related to electrical systems or industrial automation.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.6.2.1', 'H.6.2.1', 'H', 6, 'Electrical Safety', 'Quarantine Zone', 'RACEOP', 'A quarantine zone will be designated by the Organization where prototypes may be isolated if the Technical Director considers it necessary.', 'sporting', 'recommended', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.6.2.2', 'H.6.2.2', 'H', 6, 'Electrical Safety', 'Quarantine Zone', 'RACEOP', 'Only one prototype may remain inside the quarantine zone at any given time.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.6.2.3', 'H.6.2.3', 'H', 6, 'Electrical Safety', 'Quarantine Zone', 'RACEOP', 'The prototype may only be removed from the quarantine zone with the explicit authorization of the Technical Director.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.6.2.4', 'H.6.2.4', 'H', 6, 'Electrical Safety', 'Quarantine Zone', 'RACEOP', 'The rider and mechanics from the team may enter the quarantine zone only with the explicit authorization of the Technical Director. They must wear all mandatory personal safety equipment before entering the area.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.6.3.1', 'H.6.3.1', 'H', 6, 'Electrical Safety', 'Procedure in Case of Electrical Fire in Boxes, Paddock or Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'In the event of an electrical hazard in any of the above-mentioned areas, the PAS principle (Protect, Alert, Support) must be followed.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.6.3.2', 'H.6.3.2', 'H', 6, 'Electrical Safety', 'Procedure in Case of Electrical Fire in Boxes, Paddock or Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'After ensuring personal safety, the Organization must be immediately alerted. If no official staff member is nearby, the Paddock General Office must be informed.', 'sporting', 'required', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.6.3.3', 'H.6.3.3', 'H', 6, 'Electrical Safety', 'Procedure in Case of Electrical Fire in Boxes, Paddock or Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'To facilitate the safe removal of the prototype, remove any obstacles that may hinder the intervention of the Organization. Do not move any object that could endanger yourself or others nearby.', 'sporting', 'info', 'final_event', null, false, '[]'::jsonb),
  ('H.6.3.4', 'H.6.3.4', 'H', 6, 'Electrical Safety', 'Procedure in Case of Electrical Fire in Boxes, Paddock or Pit Lane', 'RACEOP', 'Follow the instructions of the Organization at all times. This is a critical safety situation; any confrontation, obstruction or lack of cooperation may result in penalties. SECTI ON I: M ODIFICATIONS GLOSSARY SECTION I MODIFICATIONS GLOSSARY SECTI ON J: ANNEXES SECTION J ANNEXES', 'sporting', 'penalty', 'final_event', null, true, '[]'::jsonb)
on conflict (clause_key) do update set
  printed_ref = excluded.printed_ref, section = excluded.section,
  article = excluded.article, article_title = excluded.article_title,
  group_title = excluded.group_title, subteam_key = excluded.subteam_key,
  body = excluded.body, obligation = excluded.obligation,
  criticality = excluded.criticality, phase = excluded.phase,
  milestone_key = excluded.milestone_key,
  is_team_duty = excluded.is_team_duty, specs = excluded.specs;

